{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b5ab-8e39-7749-9339-a8b603adb292","session_id":"01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a936eb2caa3f53","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   2→import path from 'node:path'\n   3→import { loadConfig, defaultHome, readUsage, appendUsage } from './config.mjs'\n   4→import { providerStatus } from './availability.mjs'\n   5→import { listModels, selectModels, SCHEMA as SELECT_SCHEMA } from './select.mjs'\n   6→import { forecast, estimateCost } from './forecast.mjs'\n   7→\n   8→function out(x) { process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(x, null, 2) + '\\n') }\n   9→function fail(message, code = 1) { process.stderr.write(`ERROR: ${message}\\n`); process.exit(code) }\n  10→function arg(name, fallback) { const i = process.argv.indexOf(name); return i >= 0 ? process.argv[i + 1] : fallback }\n  11→function flag(name) { return process.argv.includes(name) }\n  12→function usageFile(config) { return path.join(config._home || defaultHome(), 'usage.jsonl') }\n  13→\n  14→function load() {\n  15→  try { return loadConfig({ file: arg('--config') }) } catch (e) { fail(e.message) }\n  16→}\n  17→\n  18→function main() {\n  19→  const cmd = process.argv[2]\n  20→  const sub = process.argv[3]\n  21→  const config = load()\n  22→  if (cmd === 'providers') {\n  23→    const status = providerStatus(config)\n  24→    out({ schema: 'cliworker.providers/v1', providers: Object.entries(config.providers).map(([id, p]) => ({ id, cli: p.cli, readonly: !!p.readonly, ...status[id] })) })\n  25→    return\n  26→  }\n  27→  if (cmd === 'models' && (!sub || sub === 'list')) {\n  28→    const status = providerStatus(config)\n  29→    out({ schema: 'cliworker.models/v1', models: listModels(config, { status, includeDeprecated: flag('--all') }) })\n  30→    return\n  31→  }\n  32→  if (cmd === 'models' && sub === 'select') {\n  33→    let req = {}\n  34→    const raw = arg('--request')\n  35→    if (raw) { try { req = JSON.parse(raw) } catch (e) { fail(`bad --request JSON: ${e.message}`) } }\n  36→    const status = providerStatus(config)\n  37→    out(selectModels(config, req, { status, usage: readUsage(usageFile(config)) }))\n  38→    return\n  39→  }\n  40→  if (cmd === 'models' && sub === 'forecast') {\n  41→    const key = arg('--model', null)\n  42→    const usage = readUsage(usageFile(config))\n  43→    out({ schema: 'cliworker.forecast/v1', forecast: forecast({ records: usage, model: key, prices: key ? config.models[key]?.prices : undefined, quota: key ? config.quotas?.[config.models[key]?.provider] : null }) })\n  44→    return\n  45→  }\n  46→  if (cmd === 'usage' && sub === 'record') {\n  47→    let row\n  48→    const raw = arg('--json')\n  49→    try { row = JSON.parse(raw) } catch (e) { fail(`bad --json: ${e.message}`) }\n  50→    if (!row.model) fail('usage record requires model')\n  51→    const m = config.models[row.model]\n  52→    if (m) row.cost_usd = row.cost_usd ?? estimateCost({ input_tokens: row.input_tokens, output_tokens: row.output_tokens, prices: m.prices })\n  53→    row.at = row.at || new Date().toISOString()\n  54→    appendUsage(usageFile(config), row)\n  55→    out({ schema: 'cliworker.usage/v1', ok: true, recorded: row })\n  56→    return\n  57→  }\n  58→  if (cmd === 'usage' && sub === 'summary') {\n  59→    out({ schema: 'cliworker.usage/v1', records: readUsage(usageFile(config)) })\n  60→    return\n  61→  }\n  62→  fail('usage: cliworker providers | models list|select|forecast | usage record|summary')\n  63→}\n  64→\n  65→main()\n  66→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","_messageId":"01a1b5ab7adb7e9c9eef5630979c8cdf","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5ab7adb7e9c9eef5630979c8cdf","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5ab7adb7e9c9eef5630979c8cdf","traceparent":"00-17f4b9eb2faeae558c34db6876a0e1aa-f0f27ef812d96f38-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:01:21.594Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5ab-8e22-7a7f-bdb4-450290cf4f70","session_id":"01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b","message":{"id":"01a1b5ab8e227a7fbdb4450027e0a92a","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed:\n- `main()` auto-executes at import (line 65). `fail()` calls `process.exit`. This confirms TB-1.\n- `usageFile(config)` uses `config._home || defaultHome()` — not related to --config file path. Confirms design §1 claim.\n- `out()` writes pretty JSON (JSON.stringify with 2 spaces) — multiple lines, not \"single JSON per stdout\" strictly but still one JSON object. AC-010 says \"stdout 只输出一个 JSON\" — pretty print still one JSON object, that's fine.\n\nNow config null: line 19 `if (!raw || raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA) throw new Error(\\`unsupported CLIWorker config schema: ${raw.schema}\\`)`. \n\nTB-7 claim (1): \"null 配置 TypeError 实际来自抛错字面量里的 ${raw.schema}，raw.schema && 被 !raw 短路\". Let me verify: `!raw || ...`. If raw is null, `!raw` is true, so the whole `||` short-circuits to true WITHOUT evaluating `raw.schema && ...`. So the condition is true, and it throws `new Error(...${raw.schema}...)`. Now `raw.schema` — raw is null, so `raw.schema` throws TypeError \"Cannot read properties of null\". Yes! So the TypeError comes from the template literal `${raw.schema}` in the throw, NOT from `raw.schema &&`. Because `!raw` short-circuits the `&&` part. So TB-7 is correct about the real source.\n\nWait, but the design §1 said: \"`config.mjs` 里 `raw.schema && ...` 这行，在 raw 为 null 时会落进 `raw.schema` 读取而抛 TypeError。\" The design attributes it to `raw.schema &&` line evaluating `raw.schema`. Actually the real cause is the template literal in the throw statement. TB-7 correctly refines this: the `&&` is short-circuited by `!raw`, so the throw is entered, and the TypeError arises from `${raw.schema}` in the error message. So the fix needs to target the template literal, not the `&&`. TB-7 is correct.\n\nLet me verify the others.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","_messageId":"01a1b5ab8e227a7fbdb4450027e0a92a","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5ab8e227a7fbdb4450027e0a92a","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5ab8e227a7fbdb4450027e0a92a","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b5ab-8e22-7a7f-bdb4-450290cf4f70","traceparent":"00-17f4b9eb2faeae558c34db6876a0e1aa-f0f27ef812d96f38-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:01:32.189Z"}
