ommand\":\"git ls-files && cat package.json .gitignore && ls -la .collab && find .collab -type f | head -50\",\"description\":\"List tracked files and package metadata\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":13406,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":20798,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":13406},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fb48192a-fb8b-4a3d-b8f0-8bb0b4cd0c4f\",\"uuid\":\"77c9b2cc-02f8-4722-9302-b4d4361a2bdf\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-07T10:42:30.337Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgoRntWAhvskgvLap8rEr\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_013yXwhSyqaBjvPA2Ty7Luwt\":{\"command\":\"cd /c/git/dsh-CLIWorker && git ls-files && cat package.json .gitignore && ls -la .collab && find .collab -type f | head -50\",\"description\":\"List tracked files and package metadata\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_013yXwhSyqaBjvPA2Ty7Luwt\":{\"cwd\":\"/c/git/dsh-CLIWorker\"}}}\n 101→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","_messageId":"01a1b5acd9fc7ff8b9b1013e4ae82079","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5acd9fc7ff8b9b1013e4ae82079","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5acd9fc7ff8b9b1013e4ae82079","traceparent":"00-17f4b9eb2faeae558c34db6876a0e1aa-f0f27ef812d96f38-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:02:49.307Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5ac-e4bd-7f95-8ede-9a1ef9ad48f6","session_id":"01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b","message":{"id":"01a1b5ace4bd7f958ede9a1cbb268f34","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full requirements (sections A-F). Key observations for my review:\n\nSection F has a hard constraint: \"正文里禁止出现 ASCII 双引号字符（U+0022）\". But that's for the designer's output format, not my concern directly.\n\nAlso important: \"task_graph 的每个任务都必须齐备 id / title / inputs / outputs / write_scope / depends_on / acceptance / acceptance_direction / test_levels\". Let me verify the task graph has all these fields — it does from the prompt.\n\n\"AC 必须双向覆盖\" — every AC must be covered by tasks, and every task's acceptance must map to ACs. Let me verify this via the acceptance matrix.\n\nNow let me think about my role as reviewer. I need to produce a verdict (pass or revise) and findings. The test_architect already found 10 open blockers (TB-1..TB-10) and 3 resolved (TB-11..TB-13). My job as reviewer is to assess the design + task graph + acceptance matrix + test architecture holistically.\n\nLet me think about what a good reviewer does:\n1. Verify the design's factual claims against the code (I did several).\n2. Check internal consistency of design/interfaces/task graph/acceptance matrix.\n3. Evaluate whether the test architect's blockers are valid (and possibly dispute some).\n4. Find issues the test architect missed.\n5. Decide verdict: pass or revise.\n\nGiven TB-1 through TB-10 are all open and are legitimate structural issues, the verdict should almost certainly be \"revise\". The design is ambitious and well thought out, but there are real gaps.\n\nLet me now do a careful analysis to produce high-quality findings. Let me identify the key issues, both from the TBs and my own analysis.\n\nLet me first verify some consistency issues in the acceptance matrix and task graph.\n\n**Acceptance matrix consistency check:**\n\nLet me check the task→AC mapping. Looking at the acceptance matrix:\n- It maps each AC → tasks. Let me check whether each task's `acceptance` list matches the matrix.\n\nT-001: AC-001, AC-002. Matrix: AC-001→T-001, AC-002→T-001. ✓\nT-002: AC-003. ✓\nT-003: AC-004, AC-005, AC-006. ✓\nT-004: AC-007, AC-008. ✓\nT-005: AC-009, AC-010. ✓\nT-006: AC-011, AC-012. ✓\nT-007: AC-013, AC-014, AC-015. ✓\nT-008: AC-016, AC-017. ✓\nT-009: AC-019, AC-020. Matrix: AC-019→T-009,T-019,T-020; AC-020→T-009. ✓\nT-010: AC-021. ✓\nT-011: AC-022. ✓\nT-012: AC-023, AC-024, AC-025, AC-026. ✓\nT-013: AC-027, AC-028. ✓\nT-014: AC-029, AC-030. ✓\nT-015: AC-031, AC-032. ✓\nT-016: AC-033, AC-034. ✓\nT-017: AC-035, AC-036, AC-037, AC-038. ✓\nT-018: AC-018, AC-039, AC-040, AC-041, AC-042, AC-043. ✓\nT-019: AC-044, AC-045, AC-019. ✓\nT-020: AC-046, AC-047, AC-048, AC-019. ✓\nT-021: AC-049, AC-050. ✓\nT-022: AC-051, AC-052. ✓\nT-023: AC-053, AC-054. ✓\nT-024: AC-055. ✓\n\nOK, consistent.\n\n**Levels consistency (TB-10):** The acceptance matrix has an `levels` column and `task_levels`. Let me check a few:\n- AC-001 levels=unit, T-001 test_levels=[unit]. OK\n- AC-043 levels=contract, T-018:contract,integration,unit. Contains contract. OK.\n- AC-055 levels=smoke, T-024:smoke,unit. Contains smoke. OK.\n- AC-024 levels=unit, T-012:integration,unit. Contains unit. OK.\n\nSo the \"levels\" vs \"task_levels\" mismatch TB-10 mentions isn't strictly a mismatch — AC levels is a subset of task_levels generally. Let me check all:\n- AC-005 levels=unit, T-003:integration,unit → contains unit ✓\n- AC-006 levels=unit ✓\n- AC-009 levels=unit, T-005:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-011 levels=contract, T-006:contract ✓\n- AC-013 levels=integration,unit, T-007:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-014 levels=unit, T-007:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-015 levels=unit ✓\n- AC-016 levels=integration,unit, T-008:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-017 ✓\n- AC-018 levels=unit, T-018:contract,integration,unit ✓\n- AC-019 levels=integration, T-009:integration,unit;T-019:integration;T-020:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-020 levels=unit, T-009:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-021 levels=unit, T-010:unit ✓\n- AC-022 levels=integration, T-011:integration ✓\n- AC-023 levels=integration,unit, T-012:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-025 levels=integration, T-012:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-026 levels=integration ✓\n- AC-027 levels=unit, T-013:unit ✓\n- AC-033 levels=integration, T-016:integration ✓\n- AC-035..038 levels=unit, T-017:unit ✓\n- AC-039,040 levels=unit, T-018:contract,integration,unit ✓\n- AC-041 levels=contract,unit, T-018 has both ✓\n- AC-042 levels=integration, T-018 has integration ✓\n- AC-044,045 levels=integration, T-019:integration ✓\n- AC-046,047,048 levels=integration,unit / integration — T-020:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-049 levels=unit, T-021:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-050 levels=integration ✓\n- AC-051 levels=e2e, T-022:e2e,integration ✓\n- AC-052 levels=e2e,integration ✓\n- AC-053 levels=integration, T-023:integration,unit ✓\n- AC-054 levels=unit ✓\n- AC-055 levels=smoke, T-024:smoke,unit ✓\n\nSo actually every AC's levels are a subset of the union of task_levels. TB-10's claim \"AC-024 的 levels 与 T-012 也不完全对齐\" — hmm, AC-024 levels=unit, T-012:integration,unit. That does contain unit. So actually TB-10's claim about AC-024 might be wrong. Let me re-read TB-10: \"AC-043 标 contract 而 T-018 的 test_levels 含 4 级\". Actually T-018 has 3 levels: contract,integration,unit. Hmm, the matrix says \"T-018:contract,integration,unit\" — 3, not 4. OK.\n\nActually TB-10 is about \"level→目录的规范映射\" and traceability. It's a valid process concern but the \"不一致\" claims are partly imprecise. Let me note this as something I could dispute or refine. Actually as a reviewer I should focus on real issues.\n\nLet me think about more substantive design problems that I, as reviewer, can find. Let me brainstorm:\n\n**Issue 1: The \"包装调用\" (wrapped call) design conflicts with section B.6 and the existing AgentLine integration.**\n\nSection B.6 says: \"用户请求 CLI 时返回可直接执行的调用方式，并且带上选定的 model\". The design resolves this by putting direct calls ONLY in `cli resolve` and `view:'full'` (management entry). But B.6 says \"用户请求 CLI 时\" (when user requests CLI) — the design splits: AgentLine gets wrapped calls, management gets direct calls. Is this a faithful interpretation? The design says \"直接调用另走管理入口...只给人和管理界面用\". This seems like a reasonable design decision given D boundary (AgentLine shouldn't see provider details). But there's a subtlety: B.6 explicitly requires \"带上选定的 model\" (with the selected model). The wrapped call `node cliworker.mjs run --lease <id>` does NOT contain the model — the model is hidden behind the lease. So for the AgentLine path, B.6's \"带上选定的 model\" is NOT satisfied. The design addresses this only via `cli resolve` for management. Is that acceptable? It's a design choice that arguably reinterprets B.6. This is worth flagging as a requirement-coverage ambiguity — but the design explicitly acknowledges it in §0. It's a \"待确认\" essentially. Actually §13 assumptions don't mention this. Hmm.\n\nActually wait — let me reconsider. There's a deeper issue: the wrapped `run --lease` approach means AgentLine executes `node <pkg>/bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease <id> --config <cfg>`. This requires:\n- The CLIWorker package to be installed at a stable path accessible to AgentLine.\n- The lease to be persisted and resolvable across processes.\n- The `run` command to look up the lease from state_dir (derived from --config).\n\nThis is a significant architectural change from the current \"return a command to execute\" to \"return a token that resolves to a command\". It introduces a stateful dependency: AgentLine must call `calls[]` while the lease is still valid (not expired, not consumed). The design has `expires_at` and lease TTL (7200s). If AgentLine delays or the lease expires mid-queue, `E_LEASE_EXPIRED`. This adds a failure mode that D's \"按顺序调用\" doesn't account for. Also `count > 1` with sequential calls — leases could expire between calls. This is a real reliability concern not fully addressed. Worth a finding.\n\nAlso: **idempotency vs \"按顺序调用\"**. D says AgentLine calls calls[] in order. With wrapped calls, each call is a separate process (`node cliworker.mjs run --lease X`). If a call is retried (AgentLine retries), `run` must be idempotent per lease — the design has `E_LEASE_CONSUMED` for already-successful. Good. But what about \"重试不重复扣减\" (E6) — handled. OK.\n\n**Issue 2: `view:'full'` leakage via HTTP `/cliworker/select`.**\n\nSection D: AgentLine shouldn't see provider details. The design says `view:'full'` only available in management CLI and UI. But interfaces.md §1 says entry includes \"HTTP POST /cliworker/select\" for ModelRequest v1. Interfaces §3 says `view:'full'` (仅管理 CLI 与 UI). But the HTTP route `/cliworker/select` — is it management or AgentLine-facing? The compatibility routes (providers, models, select, forecast) currently return FULL details (provider, prices, etc.) — see lib/index.js. The design says \"保留四条兼容路由\" (keep 4 compatibility routes). If these stay as-is (returning provider/model/price details), then ANY client hitting `/cliworker/select` gets provider details — which contradicts the hard boundary D \"CLIWorker 要对 AgentLine 隐藏 provider 细节\". \n\nThis is a REAL inconsistency: the four compatibility routes (which currently expose `provider`, `vendor`, `prices`, `id`, `forecast`, `cli`) are being \"保留\" (retained) without specifying they must be gated to the management view or that AgentLine must not use them. AC-043 tests only the \"默认（AgentLine）视图\" from the CLI/select command. AC-046 says \"select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\" (select route output matches CLI) — which would mean the HTTP route returns the AgentLine view... but then how does the management UI get full details? Via `/cliworker/api/*`? Not specified. And the compatibility routes `providers`/`models`/`forecast` inherently expose provider details. \n\nSo there's an unresolved contradiction: D requires hiding provider details from AgentLine; the design keeps compatibility routes that expose them; AC-043 only guards the default view; AC-046 requires route output == CLI output. If CLI default = AgentLine view, then `/cliworker/select` returning AgentLine view would break the existing UI/management consumers that expect model keys. The design doesn't reconcile this. Worth a major finding.\n\nActually let me check: interfaces §11 lists compatibility routes \"GET /cliworker/providers，GET /cliworker/models，GET /cliworker/forecast?model=<key>，GET 或 POST /cliworker/select\". These are retained. And AC-046: \"四条兼容路由以及 /cliworker/api/*、/cliworker/health、/cliworker/ui 都能访问；select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\". \n\nIf \"与 CLI 一致\" means same as `cliworker models select` default (AgentLine view), then providers/models/forecast routes still leak provider/model/price details to any HTTP caller. Since D says AgentLine should not have provider logic and CLIWorker should hide provider details — but these HTTP routes are presumably for the management UI, not AgentLine. The design doesn't explicitly define WHO calls the compatibility routes. There's ambiguity about whether AgentLine uses `calls[]` from CLI or HTTP. Actually D says \"接收 calls[]\" — that's from ModelSelection. If AgentLine uses HTTP POST /cliworker/select, it gets the default view (fine). But the OTHER 3 routes leak. That's a boundary hole IF an AgentLine-like consumer can reach them. More importantly, the design says these routes are \"保留\" for compatibility with existing consumers — existing consumers (the current lib/index.js) expect full detail. So \"保留\" likely means keep returning full detail, which contradicts AC-046's \"select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\" (if CLI default is AgentLine view). \n\nThis is a genuine internal inconsistency worth flagging. I'll make it a finding.\n\n**Issue 3: `forecast` \"只加字段\" vs AC-007/AC-008 risk semantics.**\n\nDesign §6 says \"cliworker.forecast/v1 只加字段，旧的 burn_per_task 和 risk 枚举不变\" (only add fields, old burn_per_task and risk enum unchanged). The current risk enum is: unknown, exhausted, critical, low_reserve, ok. \n\nAC-007 says: \"remaining_pct 为 5 且容量已知时 risk 为 critical 或 exhausted\". With the current forecast logic, `risk` is computed from `tasks_left`. For `{remaining_pct:5, capacity_mtok:...}`, risk would be critical/exhausted. But the design §6 also adds `tasks_left` computed from percentiles (p90/p50/p25) and `burn_mtok_per_hour`, `eta_exhaust_at`, `exhausts_before_reset`. The OLD `risk` enum is derived from `tasks_left` — but now `tasks_left` is recomputed with a different formula (percentile-based). So \"risk 枚举不变\" but its INPUT changed. The design doesn't specify the threshold mapping for the new percentile-based tasks_left → risk. This relates to TB-2. Also AC-007 allows \"critical 或 exhausted\" — two possible outcomes — which is non-deterministic oracle (TB-2). \n\nAlso: forecast/v1 \"只加字段\" but the current `risk` uses `tasks_left` from `remaining_usd / burn` (cost-based) — the new one uses Mtok. That's a semantic change to an existing field, not just adding fields. \"只加字段，不删字段\" is satisfied literally but values change meaning. This is a compatibility risk (C: 沿用现有契约). Worth noting but maybe minor/major.\n\n**Issue 4: `cliworker.usage/v1` \"只加字段\" and `idempotency_key` — fine.**\n\n**Issue 5: AC-007 \"按剩余任务数排序生效\" — the sort in §7 is by pool remaining / reset hours, NOT by tasks_left.**\n\nAC-007 says \"按剩余任务数排序生效\" (sorting by remaining task count takes effect). But design §7 sorting rule #2 is `剩余量 / 距重置小时数` (remaining / hours-to-reset), NOT tasks_left. And the current code's `rank()` for Heavy uses `-(f.tasks_left ?? -1)`. So AC-007's \"按剩余任务数排序\" is about A1's original bug (sorting by tasks_left never worked). But the v2 design REPLACED that sort with a different policy. So AC-007's acceptance (a regression AC for A1) is testing a behavior that v2 explicitly changes. Conflict: AC-007 requires \"按剩余任务数排序生效\" but §7/T-018 implements a different sort. T-004 (M1) implements the forecast fix including \"按剩余任务数排序生效\", then T-018 (M4) rewrites select with a new sort. This is the \"M1 返工\" problem TB-6 describes, but more specifically it's an AC that asserts a behavior the final design abandons. Worth flagging — AC-007's oracle is inconsistent with §7.\n\nActually, reading AC-007 carefully: \"forecast 能处理四种额度形状... Heavy 请求以 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 被拒选，按剩余任务数排序生效\". This is about T-004 (M1, before the v2 selection policy). But AC-007 is level=unit, mapped to T-004 only. So it's testing the M1 intermediate state. But AC-041/039 etc. test the final M4 state. The acceptance matrix doesn't distinguish \"M1 intermediate behavior\" from \"final behavior\" — AC-007 would need to be re-asserted or retired after T-018. Since T-018's write_scope includes `lib/select.mjs` (rewriting the sort), AC-007's \"按剩余任务数排序生效\" could regress in M4 and no AC would catch it because AC-007 is only bound to T-004. This is a real traceability gap — an AC bound to an early task that a later task invalidates. Related to TB-6. Worth a finding.\n\n**Issue 6: `E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION` — interfaces §5 says \"兼容的选模拒选原因 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 只出现在 draft 视图里\".** But §3 rejected.reason enum (interfaces §2 line 8) lists: excluded, level_mismatch, level_unassigned, availability_blocked, availability_unavailable, availability_stale, deprecated, identity_unverified, identity_mismatch, readonly_unavailable, adapter_unverified, quota_low, quota_unknown_policy, reserve_protected — NO `E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION`. And AC-007 says \"Heavy 请求以 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 被拒选\". But §7 filter conditions don't include forecast exhaustion — the new policy uses quota_low / reserve_protected. So AC-007 asserts a rejection reason that the final design (§7, interfaces §2) doesn't have. Another inconsistency. Actually the designer put `E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION` only in draft view — but AC-007 (a unit AC for T-004) tests it. So it's an M1-only behavior. Same as Issue 5.\n\n**Issue 7: The `remaining_pct:5` → risk critical/exhausted derivation.**\n\nAC-007: \"remaining_pct 为 5 且容量已知时 risk 为 critical 或 exhausted\". With design §6's `remaining_mtok = cap*(1-used_p)`, if `remaining_pct:5` means used_p=0.95 → remaining = cap*0.05. To get `risk` critical/exhausted we need `tasks_left <= 2`. But `tasks_left` depends on burn per task (percentile) AND remaining_mtok. With capacity unknown-but-given, if capacity is large, remaining could be large → tasks_left large → risk ok. So \"remaining_pct=5 → critical/exhausted\" is NOT guaranteed by the formula; it depends on capacity and burn. Actually the design §6 says \"容量未知时... 报 unknown\". AC-007 says \"remaining_pct 为 5 且容量已知时 risk 为 critical 或 exhausted\". This requires a specific threshold definition for how pct maps to risk. The design doesn't define a `remaining_pct → risk` direct mapping; it defines `remaining_mtok → tasks_left → risk`. So AC-007's oracle is under-specified — TB-2. Confirmed.\n\n**Issue 8: `unknown_policy` and AC-008.**\n\nAC-008: \"缺容量或缺样本时 risk 保持 unknown 并给出 reason\". Reason field. interfaces §8 forecast has `reason:null`. OK. But §6 says \"没有样本时用配置估计值，并标为 assumed\" for tasks_left. So with no samples but config estimate, tasks_left is computed (assumed) — then risk would be computed from tasks_left, NOT unknown. Contradiction: AC-008 says \"缺样本 → risk unknown\", but §6 says \"没有样本时用配置估计值\" → tasks_left known → risk known. These conflict. Let me re-read §6: \"tasks_left（Heavy、Normal、Light 分别用 p90、p50、p25；没有样本时用配置估计值，并标为 assumed）\". And AC-008: \"缺容量或缺样本时 risk 保持 unknown 并给出 reason，不会用默认值算出 ok\". \n\nSo there's a direct contradiction: §6 says no samples → use config estimate (`policy.usage_estimate_mtok`) and mark assumed; AC-008 says no samples → risk stays unknown. Which wins? The design says \"缺样本一律显示 unknown，不显示 0 或 100%\" (§9, for UI). And §6 \"unknown 状态不伪造\" (E4). But §6 explicitly says use config estimate for tasks_left when no samples. This is a genuine inconsistency in the design itself. Worth a finding (major). Actually this is important — it affects the core \"unknown 不伪造\" requirement (E4, C). Let me flag.\n\nHmm, let me re-read AC-008: \"缺容量或缺样本时 risk 保持 unknown 并给出 reason，不会用默认值算出 ok\". So config estimate (`usage_estimate_mtok`) IS a \"默认值\". AC-008 says don't use it to compute ok. But §6 says use it for tasks_left marked assumed. Possibly reconcilable: tasks_left is \"assumed\" but risk stays unknown? But risk is derived from tasks_left in current code. Confusing. Definitely needs clarification. This is a good reviewer finding.\n\n**Issue 9: `importance` and `require_readonly` — fine.**\n\n**Issue 10: AC-043 forbidden-word scan vs `calls[]` containing `cliworker.mjs run --lease`.**\n\nAC-043: default view must not contain \"cli、provider、vendor、模型 id、价格、额度、forecast 或直接 CLI 命令\". The wrapped call `node <pkg>/bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease l_x --config <cfg>` — is `cliworker.mjs` a \"直接 CLI 命令\"? It's a wrapper command, not a provider CLI. And `--config <cfg>` — the config path could contain a username like `C:/Users/u/.cliworker/config.json` — that's a path, not provider detail. The `handle` has `level:'Top'`, `label:'Top-1'`. OK. But the wrapped call contains `--config C:/Users/u/.cliworker/config.json` which reveals the filesystem path and that it's CLIWorker. The scan checks for \"模型 id\" — but `claude-sonnet-5-5` might appear in... no, handle_id is opaque `h_9f2c`. OK.\n\nBut here's a subtle issue: AC-043 says the recursive scan checks \"键和值\" (keys and values) for forbidden words. The word \"cli\" as a substring — would `cliworker.mjs` or `--config` contain \"cli\"? \"cliworker\" contains \"cli\"! So a naive substring scan for \"cli\" would flag the wrapped call `cliworker.mjs`. The scan must be a key-name/token match, not a raw substring. The design says \"确认不出现 cli、provider、vendor、模型 id...\" — this is ambiguous about whether it's substring or field-name matching. AC-043 + the contract test need to define the exact matcher. TB-8 mentions \"递归扫描器若无 canary 元测试，自身失效也不会被发现\" — the canary point. But the substring collision with `cliworker` is a concrete design flaw in the AC. Worth flagging as a minor/major finding: the forbidden-word list includes \"cli\" which collides with the mandatory wrapped command `.../bin/cliworker.mjs ... --config ...`; the scan semantics must be defined (field-name/whole-token, allowlist for the wrapper) or AC-043 is unsatisfiable as written.\n\nAlso \"直接 CLI 命令\" vs wrapped command — the scan needs to allow the wrapper. Good finding.\n\n**Issue 11: `shortfall` / `truncated` vs error `E_INSUFFICIENT_QUOTA`.**\n\n§3: \"一个都没有时返回 ok:false，错误码为 E_NO_CANDIDATE 或 E_INSUFFICIENT_QUOTA\". But interfaces §2 failure example shows `shortfall:2` with ok:false. And AC-041: \"一个都没有时返回 ok:false 和 E_NO_CANDIDATE 或 E_INSUFFICIENT_QUOTA\". Two possible error codes — non-deterministic oracle (TB-2 again). Also \"可能带 retry_after\". OK.\n\n**Issue 12: `count > 1` and `calls[i]` 1:1 with `models[i]`.**\n\nAC-041: \"models 与 calls 一一对应\". interfaces §3: \"calls[i] 与 models[i].call 完全相同\". Fine.\n\n**Issue 13: `exclude_handles` + `request_id` for re-application.**\n\n§3: \"AgentLine 用新的 request_id 加 exclude_handles 再申请\". But interfaces §2 `rejected` uses `ref:'c3'` — opaque references. And `exclude_handles` refers to handles, but rejected gives `ref` (candidate refs), not handles. If a candidate is rejected, AgentLine gets `ref`, but to exclude it next time it would need `exclude_handles` with handle_ids — but rejected models don't have handles (they weren't selected). So there's a mismatch: `exclude_handles` excludes previously-returned handles (for truncated shortfall re-application), but rejected refs are a different namespace. Actually §3 says \"数量不足...用新的 request_id 加 exclude_handles 再申请\" — that's for shortfall (exclude the already-given handles to get different ones). That's consistent: when truncated, you got some handles; exclude them to get more. OK. But the `ref` in rejected is a candidate ref — could AgentLine need to exclude those? Not necessarily. OK, maybe fine.\n\n**Issue 14: `lease` + `exclude_handles` + concurrency — AC-042.**\n\nAC-042: \"50 个并发选模请求不会让同一池的预留总量超过剩余量；相同 request_id 重放返回相同 handle\". With wrapped calls, selection creates leases with soft reservations. If AgentLine requests count=2 and gets truncated:true shortfall=1, it re-applies with request_id + exclude_handles. But the leases from the first request are still reserved (not yet consumed). If the second request also reserves, total reserved could double-count. The design doesn't address how re-application interacts with existing reservations. Minor.\n\n**Issue 15: `state_dir` derivation and `--config` — AC-004.**\n\nAC-004: \"state_dir = 显式 state_dir 优先，否则 CLIWORKER_HOME/state/<配置路径摘要>\". interfaces §10: \"state_dir 未给出时取 CLIWORKER_HOME/state/<配置绝对路径 sha256 前 12 位>；相对路径按配置文件所在目录解析\". But `bin/cliworker.mjs` (the shell) and `lib/index.js` use different default config paths. Let me check bin/cliworker.mjs.\n\nLet me read bin/cliworker.mjs.\n\nActually, I should check this. Let me read it.\n\n**Issue 16: `T-005` builds `errors.mjs` 初版, `T-006` replaces with registry — but `T-005` also creates `lib/commands/**` migrating existing commands, and `T-006` creates `lib/contract/**`. The `write_scope` of T-005 includes `lib/contract/errors.mjs` and T-006 includes `lib/contract/**`. Overlapping write scopes across milestones — acceptable but note.\n\n**Issue 17: `depends_on` cycles / ordering.**\n\nLet me verify the dependency graph is acyclic and all referenced IDs exist. Let me check:\n- T-001: []\n- T-002: [T-001]\n- T-003: [T-001]\n- T-004: [T-001]\n- T-005: [T-003, T-004]\n- T-006: [T-005]\n- T-007: [T-003]\n- T-008: [T-001]\n- T-009: [T-003, T-007, T-008]\n- T-010: [T-003, T-009]\n- T-011: [T-008]\n- T-012: [T-007, T-008, T-010, T-011]\n- T-013: [T-009, T-012]\n- T-014: [T-006, T-012]\n- T-015: [T-010, T-013]\n- T-016: [T-011, T-014, T-015]\n- T-017: [T-004, T-007, T-015]\n- T-018: [T-006, T-016, T-017]\n- T-019: [T-009, T-014, T-018]\n- T-020: [T-007, T-009, T-018, T-019]\n- T-021: [T-020]\n- T-022: [T-002, T-019, T-020]\n- T-023: [T-019, T-021, T-022]\n- T-024: [T-022, T-023]\n\nAll references exist. Acyclic (IDs increase). Good. But note: T-019 depends on T-018 which depends on T-017 which depends on T-015 which depends on T-013 which depends on T-012 which depends on T-010 which depends on T-009 which depends on T-007/T-008/T-003. And T-014 depends on T-006, T-012. T-016 depends on T-014, T-015, T-011. Fine.\n\nBut here's a **milestone mismatch**: T-019 (M4) depends on T-014 (M3) and T-018 (M4) — fine. T-020 (M5) depends on T-019 (M4). Fine. T-022 (M5) depends on T-002 (M1). Fine.\n\nHowever: **T-007 (M2) depends only on T-003 (M1)** — good. **T-008 (M2) depends only on T-001 (M1)** — good. But T-009 (M2) depends on T-007, T-008 (both M2) and T-003 — fine. T-010 (M2) depends on T-009 (M2) — fine. T-011 (M2) depends on T-008 — fine. T-012 (M3) depends on T-010, T-011 (M2) — fine.\n\n**But T-016 (M3) depends on T-015 (M3), T-014 (M3), T-011 (M2)** — fine.\n\nOK.\n\n**Critical dependency issue**: T-017 (M4) depends on T-015 (M3) — but §6/§11 says A1 fix \"先在 lib/quota.mjs 把四种额度形状统一成 Mtok\" is T-004 (M1), and \"M4 在这个基础上扩展成多池模型\". T-017 depends on T-004 ✓.\n\n**Issue 18: AC-018 \"选模只读缓存状态：注入 exec 探针断言选模过程中 0 次子进程\" — but `providerStatus` is called in `lib/cli.mjs` `models select` BEFORE `selectModels`.** In the current code, `main()` calls `providerStatus(config)` (which spawns) then `selectModels`. The v2 design says \"选模不起任何子进程\" and availability is read from `state_dir/probes.json`. So T-018 must ensure the CLI select command doesn't call providerStatus. But T-005 (M1) migrates commands and T-016 (M3) rewrites availability.mjs to read cache. Between M1 and M3, `models select` would still spawn. AC-018 is bound to T-018 (M4) so it's tested at the end. OK. But this reinforces TB-1 (import-safe, injectable) — the exec probe requires injection. Fine.\n\n**Issue 19: `check-fast.ps1` relies on `pwsh` — TB-4.** Let me verify pwsh availability. Actually I can't run commands. The env says platform win32, default shell bash. Windows 11 Home China. PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell.exe`) is available but `pwsh` (PowerShell 7) may not be. The design says `scripts/check-fast.ps1` and AC-002 \"pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/check-fast.ps1\". The acceptance_direction for T-001 says \"pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/check-fast.ps1\". If `pwsh` isn't installed on Windows 11 Home China (common — PowerShell 7 is not bundled), this command fails. TB-4 flags this. Let me verify by checking if pwsh exists — but I can't run commands. I can note it as a risk. Actually the PowerShell tool I was denied. Hmm. Let me note it as a finding but with appropriate uncertainty — TB-4 already covers it. Actually, I should verify: the environment says \"Default shell: bash\" and the PowerShell tool description says \"Edition: Windows PowerShell 5.1 (powershell.exe)\". That strongly suggests `powershell.exe` (5.1) is present but `pwsh` (7) is NOT necessarily. The design's `pwsh` assumption is unverified. But TB-4 covers this. I'll consolidate.\n\nActually, I can check via Glob for pwsh? No. Let me not over-invest.\n\n**Issue 20: AC-001 \"Node 20 和 Node 22 上都以 0 退出\"** — no CI config in the task graph. The design §11 says `npm test` = `node scripts/run-tests.mjs test`. T-001 outputs `package.json scripts（test、test:unit、test:contract、check）`. But there's no CI workflow file in any write_scope, and no task for CI. AC-001 requires Node 20 AND 22 — that's a matrix, which needs CI config (e.g., `.github/workflows/`). TB-3/TB-4 flag this: \"当前又无任何 CI 配置，双 Node 版本矩阵无处运行\". So AC-001's \"在 Node 20 和 Node 22 上都以 0 退出\" has no enforcement mechanism in the task graph. This is a real gap. Worth a finding.\n\n**Issue 21: AC-055 \"真机冒烟\" as a release gate with \"任何 fail 都阻断发布\" but no release process / no task owns the gate.** TB-9. Also \"test_levels: smoke,unit\" but no `test/smoke/` dir. TB-10. And AC-055's acceptance_direction uses PowerShell syntax `$env:CLIWORKER_SMOKE='1'` — again pwsh assumption. Also the design §13 assumption #3 says probes consume quota and default manual — but AC-055 requires running probe on real machine. OK.\n\n**Issue 22: The example config `config/cliworker.example.json` has NO `schema` field.** Look at it — it starts with `providers`, no `schema`. But `lib/config.mjs` `loadConfig` checks `if (!raw || raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA)`. Since `raw.schema` is undefined, `undefined && ...` = falsy, so no throw. So example loads fine currently. The v2 design wants `_example:true` added so loading example returns `E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE` (AC-005). But interfaces §10 says v2 config has `schema:'cliworker.config/v2'`. If v1 config has `schema:'cliworker.config/v1'`, and the example has NO schema — then loading the example under v2 would... hmm. AC-021 says \"v1 配置在内存中迁移为 v2 并给出 W_CONFIG_V1\". A config with no schema — is it v1? The current `loadConfig` accepts it. The design doesn't specify how schema-less configs are classified in v2. Minor.\n\nAlso AC-005 says \"example 带 _example:true，直接加载 example 或与之逐字节相同的配置返回 E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE\". \"与之逐字节相同的配置\" — detecting byte-identical config requires hashing the file content and comparing to the example. That's an unusual mechanism (why would a user's real config be byte-identical to example? because the current `config/cliworker.local.json` IS byte-identical to example — A4 says so). So the check is meant to catch the placeholder local config. But how does CLIWorker know the example's bytes at runtime? The example is shipped in the package (`config/cliworker.example.json`) — so it can hash it. But if installed via npm pack, the path is known. OK, feasible. But \"逐字节相同\" is brittle (whitespace changes defeat it). Minor.\n\n**Issue 23: `T-003` write_scope includes `lib/config.mjs` and `test/unit/config.test.mjs`, but AC-006 (null config TypeError) — TB-7 (1) says the real cause is the template literal `${raw.schema}` in the throw on line 19, not the `raw.schema &&` condition.** I verified: line 19 `if (!raw || raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA) throw new Error(\\`unsupported CLIWorker config schema: ${raw.schema}\\`)`. When raw is null: `!raw` is true → short-circuit → throw → template literal evaluates `raw.schema` → TypeError. So the fix must guard the template literal. The design §1 says the problem is \"raw.schema && ... 这行...会落进 raw.schema 读取而抛 TypeError\" — which mislocates the cause (it's the throw message, not the `&&`). TB-7 is correct. This is a design errata that affects AC-006's \"修复点须对准真实行\". Worth including as a finding (I can validate TB-7). \n\nAlso note: `loadConfig` catches JSON parse errors and throws E_CONFIG, but the `throw new Error(...)` on line 19/20/21 is NOT wrapped with `error.code = 'E_CONFIG'`. AC-006 says \"返回 E_CONFIG 和包含文件路径与原因的可读信息\". Currently only the read/parse failure gets `E_CONFIG`; schema/validation failures throw plain Error with no code. So T-003 must add codes to all validation throws. The design §1 doesn't mention this. Minor but part of AC-006.\n\n**Issue 24: `forecast` 3 call sites vs comparator — TB-7 (3).** I verified: 3 sites (filter line 94, rank line 102, picked line 116), and `rank` is called inside `candidates.sort` comparator → O(n log n) calls, each recomputing forecast. So \"每个候选模型的 forecast 只计算一次\" (AC-009) requires memoization keyed by model. The design §1 says \"在过滤、排序、输出三处各调一次\" (3 calls) — which understates it (comparator multiplies). TB-7 correct. AC-009's \"注入计数器断言\" needs to count calls, and the design's \"去掉重复 forecast\" (T-005) must implement memoization, not just remove 2 of 3 sites. Worth a finding.\n\n**Issue 25: `.gitignore` — TB-7 (2).** I verified: only literal lines. AC-005 requires wildcard `config/*.local.json`, `state/`, `*.jsonl`. The design §11 lists \"修正后的 .gitignore\" as a T-003 output. So it's planned. But note: `config/cliworker.example.json` is NOT ignored (good, it must be shipped in npm pack per AC-003). With a rule `config/*.local.json`, example isn't matched. Good. But `*.jsonl` would match any jsonl anywhere including `test/fixtures/*.jsonl` if they add fixtures with .jsonl — could accidentally ignore test fixtures. Minor.\n\n**Issue 26: AC-003 \"npm pack 产物包含 bin/cliworker.mjs、config/cliworker.example.json、lib/ 和 package.json 中的 bin.cliworker\".** T-002 outputs `files`: `bin、lib、config/cliworker.example.json、ui、contracts、cordis.patch.yml、dsh.plugin.json、README.md`. But `README.md` and `package.json` are always included by npm. `bin/cliworker.mjs` — need `bin` entry AND `files` includes `bin`. OK. But `scripts/` is NOT in `files` — that's fine for runtime (dev scripts). But `scripts/check-pack.mjs` is referenced by T-002 as an output — it's not shipped, fine. However, `docs/` is NOT in `files`, yet `docs/migration.md` etc. are created by T-006/T-023. AC-053 `check-docs` runs README/docs commands — those run from the repo, not the packed package. OK. But if users install via npm and need `docs/`, they won't have it. Not required. Minor.\n\n**Issue 27: `bin/cliworker.mjs` — let me read it to check the entry.** Let me read it.\n\nActually let me read bin/cliworker.mjs and README to complete the picture.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","_messageId":"01a1b5ace4bd7f958ede9a1cbb268f34","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5ace4bd7f958ede9a1cbb268f34","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5ace4bd7f958ede9a1cbb268f34","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b5ac-e4bd-7f95-8ede-9a1ef9ad48f6","traceparent":"00-17f4b9eb2faeae558c34db6876a0e1a