{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b5af-a55a-7b3e-9dcb-c2b525744d01","session_id":"01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdefed5d41d4337d","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→# CLIWorker\n   2→\n   3→AgentLine 的独立模型层。AgentLine 只保留“模型来源”指针；provider/CLI、模型列举、可用性、价格、用量与预测全部由 CLIWorker 负责。\n   4→\n   5→## 边界\n   6→\n   7→```text\n   8→AgentLine  --ModelRequest JSON-->  CLIWorker  --ModelSelection JSON-->  AgentLine\n   9→```\n  10→\n  11→- AgentLine 不读取 provider CLI、不维护价格表、不做预测。\n  12→- CLIWorker 可以独立安装、替换、禁用。\n  13→- AgentLine 的 `modelSource` 只保存 CLIWorker 的启动配置。\n  14→\n  15→## CLI\n  16→\n  17→```bash\n  18→node bin/cliworker.mjs providers\n  19→node bin/cliworker.mjs models list\n  20→node bin/cliworker.mjs models list --all\n  21→node bin/cliworker.mjs models select --request '{\"role\":\"dev\",\"tier\":\"top\",\"count\":2,\"importance\":\"high\"}'\n  22→node bin/cliworker.mjs models forecast --model hy4free\n  23→node bin/cliworker.mjs usage record --json '{\"model\":\"hy4free\",\"input_tokens\":1000,\"output_tokens\":500}'\n  24→node bin/cliworker.mjs usage summary\n  25→```\n  26→\n  27→所有输出都是 JSON。\n  28→\n  29→## 配置\n  30→\n  31→默认配置：`$CLIWORKER_HOME/config.json`（默认 `~/.cliworker/config.json`）。  \n  32→参考 `config/cliworker.example.json`。\n  33→\n  34→配置包含：\n  35→\n  36→- providers：CLI、adapter、版本/认证命令、是否可强制只读\n  37→- models：provider、id、tier、identity、vendor、价格、弃用\n  38→- quotas：各渠道剩余额度/窗口\n  39→\n  40→## AgentLine 集成\n  41→\n  42→AgentLine 仅保存：\n  43→\n  44→```json\n  45→\"modelSource\": {\n  46→  \"kind\": \"cliworker\",\n  47→  \"command\": \"node\",\n  48→  \"args\": [\"C:/git/dsh-CLIWorker/bin/cliworker.mjs\", \"--config\", \"C:/git/dsh-CLIWorker/config/cliworker.local.json\"]\n  49→}\n  50→```\n  51→\n  52→选模时调用：\n  53→\n  54→```text\n  55→cliworker models select --request <ModelRequest>\n  56→```\n  57→\n  58→返回的 `models[]` 是 `ModelHandle[]`，AgentLine 按顺序尝试。\n  59→\n  60→## 安全\n  61→\n  62→- 未验证 identity、不可调用、弃用模型不会出现在候选中。\n  63→- `rejected[]` 保留原因，便于审计。\n  64→- 预测缺样本返回 `unknown`，不伪造通过。\n  65→\n  66→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","_messageId":"01a1b5af91977cb680ce7af1ad0d0d66","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5af91977cb680ce7af1ad0d0d66","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5af91977cb680ce7af1ad0d0d66","traceparent":"00-17f4b9eb2faeae558c34db6876a0e1aa-f0f27ef812d96f38-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b5aac9ec784c83c68bb8ccbd74dc"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:05:49.659Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5af-a529-79c6-bf4e-e01a98b8cc74","session_id":"01a1b5aa-c729-7df6-9d0b-469c0be45c4b","message":{"id":"01a1b5afa52979c6bf4ee018f4493c4f","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed A5: README request example has `role`, `tier`, `importance` — `role` and `importance` are silently ignored by current code. `tier` is used as level alias in `normLevel(request.level || request.tier)`. So role/importance ignored. Design §11 \"修正后的 README 请求示例\" and T-005/AC-010 address this. Good.\n\nAlso note: README's modelSource points to `bin/cliworker.mjs` with `--config` — but current `bin/cliworker.mjs` doesn't accept `--config` at the top level? Actually `arg('--config')` is read inside `load()` from process.argv, so `node bin/cliworker.mjs --config X models select` would work since `arg` searches all argv. OK.\n\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me also quickly check the reviewer.log for any prior review (maybe empty).\n\nActually, let me check if there's a prior reviewer round. state.json says phase=review, round current=1, calls has only design and testability. So this is the first reviewer call. reviewer.log might contain the current prompt. Let me check its size/content briefly — not essential. Let me skip.\n\nNow, let me also double-check the task graph JSON validity — specifically the \"AC 必须双向覆盖\" and \"depends_on 只能引用真实存在的任务 ID\". I checked. Let me also verify there are 24 tasks and 55 ACs. From the prompt: AC-001 to AC-055 = 55 ACs. Tasks T-001 to T-024 = 24. Milestones M1-M5 = 5. Good.\n\nLet me check \"AC 双向覆盖\": every AC appears in at least one task's acceptance, and every task's acceptance AC exists in the acceptance array. From the matrix, all 55 ACs are mapped. Let me check a couple that might be orphaned: AC-018 → T-018 ✓. AC-019 → T-009,T-019,T-020 ✓. All good.\n\nNow let me also check: **interfaces.md §5 error codes registry** vs AC-010 \"退出码符合注册表\" and AC-011 \"错误码注册表与快照一致，删除或改名会让测试失败\". The design T-006 outputs `contracts/error-codes.snapshot.json`. Good.\n\nBut note: **interfaces §5 includes `E_SCHEMA_UNSUPPORTED`** but config.mjs throws `unsupported CLIWorker config schema: ...` with no code. And `E_REQUEST_INVALID` etc. The errors.mjs registry (T-005 初版 → T-006 final). Fine.\n\nNow let me think about whether there's a **critical contradiction in the wrapped call design vs B.6 / D / C** that I should elevate.\n\nLet me re-read D: \"AgentLine 只负责：指定 level / count / usage；接收 calls[]；按顺序调用；数量不够时再申请；记录流程状态。\" And \"CLIWorker 要对 AgentLine 隐藏 provider 细节，只暴露 ModelRequest / ModelSelection / ModelHandle 与稳定的错误码\".\n\nB.6: \"用户请求 CLI 时返回可直接执行的调用方式，并且带上选定的 model；不同平台/CLI 的形态差异（命令、参数、只读模式、cwd、stdin）要覆盖。\"\n\nThe design's resolution: AgentLine default view → wrapped call WITHOUT model. Management (`cli resolve`, view:full) → direct call WITH model. \n\nIs B.6 satisfied? \"用户请求 CLI 时返回可直接执行的调用方式，并且带上选定的 model\". The design provides this via `cli resolve` for management/UI. But for the primary consumer (AgentLine via `models select`), the call does NOT include the model. So B.6's \"带上选定的 model\" is only satisfied in the management path. Given D explicitly says AgentLine must NOT see model details, this is arguably the only consistent resolution — you can't both hide the model from AgentLine AND include it in the call. So the design's split is a reasonable reconciliation. I'd note it as an \"assumption needing user confirmation\" rather than a defect. Actually §13 assumptions don't list it. Let me make it a finding (major) about requirement interpretation: B.6 requires the returned call to carry the selected model, but the AgentLine default view deliberately strips it (wrapped `--lease`); the design satisfies B.6 only through `cli resolve`/`view:'full'`, which is a reinterpretation that should be explicitly confirmed, and AC-029/AC-030 only test `cli resolve` not that the AgentLine `calls[]` is \"可直接执行\" with model. Hmm — actually AC-029 says \"cli resolve 返回带选定 model 的直接调用\" ✓. So B.6 is covered by AC-029. OK, so it's covered. It's more of a \"documented reinterpretation\" — maybe minor. Let me include it as a minor finding about the semantic gap, or fold it into the boundary finding.\n\nActually, there's a sharper issue: **the wrapped call requires the lease to be persisted and `run` to resolve it. But `calls[]` from `models select` (CLI mode) — when AgentLine runs `node cliworker.mjs run --lease l_x --config cfg`, a NEW process starts, loads config, and must find `leases.json` in `state_dir`. But `models select` might have been invoked via HTTP (DSH plugin), where `state_dir` is derived from the plugin's `configPath`, while the `run` process derives `state_dir` from `--config <cfg>`. If the plugin's config path and the `--config` in the call string differ, the lease won't be found.** The wrapped call hardcodes `--config <cfg>` in the handle (interfaces §3: `--config','C:/Users/u/.cliworker/config.json'`). Where does that `<cfg>` come from? It must be the SAME config path used by the selecting process. For HTTP, the plugin uses `settings.configPath` (DEFAULTS: CLIWORKER_CONFIG env or ~/.cliworker/config.json). For CLI, `arg('--config')` or default. These could differ. The design doesn't specify that the handle's `--config` is derived from the active config path (and that `state_dir` is a pure function of it). AC-004 tests that two different configs don't cross-talk, which is the same mechanism. But there's no AC that specifically tests \"a selection made via HTTP produces a `run --lease` call that can resolve the lease in a fresh process\". AC-044 tests `run --lease` with a lease presumably created in the same... Let me check AC-044: \"run --lease 以 cliworker.event/v1 JSONL 输出归一事件\". It doesn't say cross-process. AC-045 covers E_LEASE_CONSUMED. But the critical cross-process lease resolution (HTTP select → CLI run) isn't explicitly an AC. This is a real gap given it's the CORE of the wrapped-call design. Worth a finding.\n\nActually let me reconsider — AC-046 \"select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\" implies the HTTP route returns the same selection including calls[]. If AgentLine uses HTTP select and then executes calls[], the cross-process lease resolution must work. T-019/T-020 tests cover runner and plugin routes separately but not the integration. AC-051 (e2e install) tests `cliworker --version` and `doctor`, not the full select→run flow. So there's no AC for \"select → run end-to-end across process boundary\". This is a significant test gap. Worth a finding (major).\n\nLet me also reconsider the biggest-picture question: what should my verdict be? Definitely \"revise\" — there are open blockers from the test architect (TB-1..TB-10) that are legitimate and unresolved, plus my own findings. The design is high quality but needs a revision round.\n\nNow, how should I structure findings? I should:\n1. Consolidate/validate the test architect's blockers (not just repeat all 10 verbatim — but as reviewer I should acknowledge the most critical ones and either confirm or dispute).\n2. Add my own findings that the test architect missed.\n3. Possibly dispute some TBs that are imprecise.\n\nLet me think about which TBs to dispute:\n- TB-10's claim \"AC-024 的 levels 与 T-012 也不完全对齐\" — I checked, AC-024 levels=unit, T-012:integration,unit — unit ⊂, so it IS aligned by subset. The real issue TB-10 raises (level→目录映射 + traceability matrix) is valid, but the specific \"不完全对齐\" examples are weak. I could mark a finding as \"disputed\" for the imprecise parts. But as a reviewer, I think it's more constructive to note that TB-10's traceability concern is valid while some of its stated inconsistencies are not actual inconsistencies (levels is a subset of task_levels by design). Let me include a \"disputed\" finding to be precise. Actually, having a \"disputed\" status finding is appropriate — the schema allows it. Let me use it for one or two.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The reviewer's job in Blueprint is typically to review the DESIGN and produce findings that the designer will address in round 2. The test_architect's TBs are inputs. The reviewer should:\n- Endorse the valid blockers (so they get addressed).\n- Add design-level findings (consistency, requirement coverage, boundary).\n- Dispute anything overstated.\n\nLet me decide the finding set. I'll aim for ~10-14 findings, well-organized, with a mix of blocking/major/minor, and a couple of \"resolved\" (acknowledging things that are fine) and one \"disputed\".\n\nActually the schema: `{\"verdict\":\"pass|revise\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F-01\",\"severity\":\"blocking|major|minor\",\"status\":\"open|resolved|disputed\",\"text\":\"...\"}]}`. The status per-finding — I think \"open\" means the issue is open/needs fixing, \"resolved\" means already addressed (so no action), \"disputed\" means I disagree with a claim. For my own findings, status should be \"open\" (they need fixing). I can include a few \"resolved\" to note verified-correct aspects (good reviewer practice — confirms non-obvious approaches worked, like TB-11/12/13 do). And \"disputed\" for overstated TBs.\n\nLet me now think about the most important findings to include. I'll organize:\n\n**Blocking findings (must fix before implementation):**\n\nF-01 (blocking, open): Consolidate TB-1 — injectability/import-safe seam missing. This is the single biggest blocker: ~12 ACs (009/018/019/022/026/046) depend on exec/fs probes, counters, fake ctx, fake CLI, but `lib/cli.mjs` auto-runs `main()` + `fail()`→`process.exit`, `lib/availability.mjs` imports `spawnSync` directly, `lib/index.js:apply()` swallows registration errors into `console.error` (pseudo webServer test would pass vacuously). Verified against code: cli.mjs:65, cli.mjs:9, availability.mjs:1, index.js:72-74, bin/cliworker.mjs:2. Need unified `createContext` + import-safe entry in M2 before those ACs can be written. Without this, ACs can only be \"passed\" via fragile monkey-patching.\n\nF-02 (blocking, open): Contract freeze timing / milestone rework (TB-6). T-004 builds quota.mjs/forecast, T-017 rewrites both; T-005 builds errors.mjs 初版, T-006 replaces with registry+snapshot, while AC-011/041/043/045/039 depend on the latter. Also AC-007/009/010 are bound to M1 tasks but assert behaviors the M4 design changes (see below). Need T-006 to freeze contracts/examples + error-codes.snapshot.json + AgentLine forbidden-word list once, only-add-fields thereafter, with a test that deleting/renaming bumps snapshot and fails AC-011.\n\nF-03 (blocking, open): Undefined oracles / non-unique judgment values (TB-2). AC-007 allows critical OR exhausted; AC-008/039 only \"reason\"; AC-038 confidence has no formula/tolerance; AC-035 lacks Mtok unit, cap×(1−used) rounding, and exact ledger weighting formula; AC-011/039/045 rejection/failure reason enums aren't unified with error-codes.snapshot.json. Without a single frozen reason enum + threshold table + confidence formula, implementation can drift and tests can't have a unique oracle.\n\nF-04 (blocking, open): Wall-clock thresholds + no CI (TB-3/TB-4). AC-017 (N/4+1s), AC-018 (p95<300ms), AC-042/013 concurrency with sleep are machine-dependent/flaky; AC-001 requires Node 20 AND 22 but no CI config exists anywhere in the task graph (no workflow file, no task owns it). Need: replace CI assertions with structural invariants (exec count=0, reserved≤remaining, 1000 lines parse, replay idempotent), move absolute timings to an isolated perf job, add a CI matrix task + lockfile/pwsh decision.\n\n**Major findings:**\n\nF-05 (major, open): Boundary hole — compatibility routes vs default AgentLine view. D requires hiding provider details from AgentLine; the design \"保留四条兼容路由\" (providers/models/select/forecast) that currently return full provider/vendor/price/model details (verified lib/index.js:50-70), and AC-046 requires \"select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\" while AC-043 only guards the CLI default view. Unreconciled: either the compat routes must be gated to management view/full, or they leak provider details over HTTP; and if select route == CLI default view, existing UI consumers that expect model keys break. Need to specify who consumes each route, auth/gating, and add a contract test that scans HTTP responses too (AC-043 currently only covers the CLI/select default view).\n\nF-06 (major, open): Wrapped `run --lease` cross-process/lease-lifecycle gap. The core design (calls[] = `node cliworker.mjs run --lease <id> --config <cfg>`) makes selection→execution stateful: a fresh process must resolve the lease from `state_dir` derived from the `--config` in the handle. Unspecified/untested: (a) that the handle's `--config` is exactly the active config path used by the selecting process (HTTP plugin uses `settings.configPath`/CLIWORKER_CONFIG, CLI uses `--config` — these can diverge, and `lib/index.js:20` has its own default); (b) `expires_at`/lease_ttl vs D's \"按顺序调用\" with count>1 — leases may expire between sequential calls; (c) no AC covers select→run across a process boundary (AC-044/045 test runner in isolation, AC-046 tests routes, AC-051 tests only --version/doctor). Need an end-to-end AC: HTTP select → execute calls[] in a fresh process → events → lease consumed.\n\nF-07 (major, open): Internal contradiction on `unknown` semantics. AC-008 says \"缺容量或缺样本时 risk 保持 unknown…不会用默认值算出 ok\", but §6 says tasks_left falls back to config `policy.usage_estimate_mtok` when no samples (marked assumed), and E4/§9 demand \"unknown 不伪造\". With tasks_left computed, risk would be derived (ok/critical) — contradicting AC-008. Need to pin down whether assumed tasks_left still yields risk:unknown, and how `assumed` interacts with `confidence`/`status`. Also §6 \"没有样本时用配置估计值\" conflicts with §9 \"缺样本一律显示 unknown，不显示 0 或 100%\".\n\nF-08 (major, open): AC-007/AC-009 oracle vs final design drift. AC-007 asserts \"Heavy 请求以 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 被拒选，按剩余任务数排序生效\" and §3 says E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION appears only in draft view (interfaces §5), while §7's final selection policy uses `quota_low`/`reserve_protected` and sorts by `remaining_mtok / hours_to_reset`, not tasks_left; interfaces §2's rejected.reason enum has no E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION. AC-007/009 are bound to M1 tasks (T-004/T-005) whose behavior M4 (T-018) replaces, with no AC re-asserting or retiring them — so the M1 ACs can pass while the shipped behavior differs. Also AC-009 \"每个候选模型的 forecast 只计算一次\" understates reality: verified `select.mjs:94,102,116` call forecast at 3 sites AND `rank` is inside the sort comparator (`select.mjs:109`) → O(n log n) recomputations; fixing requires memoization keyed by model, not deleting 2 sites, and the injected counter must count calls not call sites. (Also validates TB-7's point 3.)\n\nF-09 (major, open): Factual errata in §1 that misdirect AC fixes (validates TB-7). (1) null-config TypeError: verified `config.mjs:19` — `!raw ||` short-circuits `raw.schema &&`, so the TypeError comes from `${raw.schema}` inside the throw's template literal, NOT from the `&&` condition; AC-006's fix must guard the error message, and all validation throws (lines 19-21) currently lack `error.code='E_CONFIG'` so AC-006's \"返回 E_CONFIG\" needs codes added. (2) `.gitignore` verified has only literal `config/cliworker.local.json` + `usage.jsonl` — no `config/*.local.json` wildcard, no `state/`, no `*.jsonl`; AC-005's git check-ignore oracle must be authored against wildcard behavior. (3) run --lease/resolve/wrapped calls don't exist yet — AC-044/045 are new features needing goldens, not regressions (characterization tests per test-strategy §2). Need a §1 errata before ACs are frozen.\n\nF-10 (major, open): Cumulative harness ownership + canary (TB-8). AC-019's sentinel scan is split across T-009→T-019→T-020; if each stage writes a local scan, later stages won't rerun the full flow and HTTP leakage escapes. AC-043's recursive scanner needs a canary meta-test (\"inject a provider field → must be caught\") or its own failure is invisible; check-docs (AC-053) and smoke report (AC-055) should reuse the same scanner. Also note the forbidden-word list contains `cli`, which collides with the mandatory wrapped command `.../bin/cliworker.mjs ... --config ...` — AC-043's scan semantics (field-name/whole-token + wrapper allowlist) must be defined or it's unsatisfiable as written.\n\nF-11 (major, open): Cross-platform skip/release-gate semantics (TB-5/TB-9/TB-10). AC-016/024/020/029 can't run natively on a single-OS CI; \"跳过并记录原因\" has no machine-readable format/baseline, and skip could be conflated with pass. AC-055 requires real machine + credentials + DSH host (not CI-runnable) yet \"任何 fail 都阻断发布\" with skip/fail relationship undefined and no owner for the gate; also there's no `test/smoke/` dir despite levels:smoke, and no fake-cli dry-run so the pipeline can execute it in CI. Need: structured skip清单, level→directory map + AC→test-file traceability (AC-001/002 + E7 objective verification), skip never counts as pass for release, CI dry-run.\n\n**Minor findings:**\n\nF-12 (minor, open): Config/schema classification gaps. Example config has no `schema` field (verified) and no `_example:true`; v1→v2 migration (AC-021) doesn't say how a schema-less config is classified, and `E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE` for \"byte-identical config\" is brittle (whitespace defeats it). AC-004's `state_dir` derivation must be a pure function of the active `--config` path shared by CLI and plugin (currently `lib/index.js:20` computes its own default) — otherwise two entry points derive different state dirs.\n\nF-13 (minor, open): Packaging/tooling details. AC-003's `files` list (T-002) omits `docs/` and `scripts/` (fine for runtime but `check-docs`/`doctor` reference them from repo only); `check-fast.ps1`/AC-002/AC-055 acceptance_direction assume `pwsh` (PowerShell 7) while this host exposes Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell.exe`) — need a fallback or explicit `pwsh` install task; `check-unused` (AC-009) has no static-analysis tool given \"零第三方依赖\" — needs an explicit decision (pinned devDependency vs narrow AST checker + self-test). (Consolidates TB-4.)\n\nF-14 (minor, open): `forecast/v1 \"只加字段\"` is not purely additive — `risk`/`tasks_left`/`burn_per_task` values change meaning from USD/cost-based to Mtok/percentile-based; C requires \"沿用现有契约\", so a semantic-change note + draft mapping is needed even if no fields are removed. Also `importance` was silently ignored in README (verified README.md:21) — AC-010/AC-053 cover it, good.\n\n**Resolved findings (verified-correct, to record as validated):**\n\nF-15 (resolved): Verified correct: deterministic forecast with fixed `now`+samples, unknown-preservation (AC-008 intent), whitelist-only probing with kind=probe ledger (AC-033/034), and the \"no fake handle\" triple constraint (call non-empty + callable/unexpired + quota passed) are all sound and give unique oracles — validates TB-11/12/13. Also verified §1's A1 claim: example quotas (`remaining_pct`, `remaining`+`unit:credits`) never satisfy forecast's `remaining_usd`/`unit==='tokens'` branches (`forecast.mjs:34,37`), so risk is always unknown — the A1 bug is real and correctly diagnosed. And cursor-wsl injection (`select.mjs:49`) and cli/call duplication (`select.mjs:123`) confirmed.\n\n**Disputed findings:**\n\nF-16 (disputed): TB-10's claimed level/traceability \"不一致\" examples are overstated as inconsistencies: every AC's `levels` is a subset of the union of its tasks' `test_levels` (e.g., AC-024 levels=unit ⊂ T-012:integration,unit; AC-043 levels=contract ⊂ T-018:contract,integration,unit; AC-001 unit ⊂ T-001 unit). The underlying asks (level→directory map, AC→test-file traceability matrix, set-equality discovery check) are valid and should be kept, but they are process improvements, not evidence of a broken matrix. Keep as minor, don't treat as a blocking inconsistency.\n\nHmm, that's 16 findings. That might be too many. Let me consolidate to ~12-14. Actually for a thorough review of a large design, 12-16 findings is reasonable. But let me make sure the JSON is valid and each finding is crisp.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the verdict and the framing. The question says \"verdict 只能是 pass 或 revise\". Given the blockers, \"revise\" is right.\n\nLet me also double check: should I include \"resolved\" findings? The test architect's testability.json has 3 resolved TBs. The reviewer output format includes status \"resolved\" — so it's intended to be used. I'll include 1-2 resolved findings to acknowledge verified-correct aspects. That's good practice and matches the memory instructions about recording confirmations.\n\nLet me reconsider F-16 (disputed). Is it worth including? It adds precision and shows I actually checked the matrix. Yes, include it — it's a genuine \"disputed\" item.\n\nNow let me be careful about one thing: I should not make the text too long per finding but must be specific with file:line references where relevant. The user asked for JSON only. Let me make the text strings in Chinese (matching the design) and include code refs.\n\nLet me also double-check a couple of my claims:\n\n1. \"lib/index.js:20 computes its own default\" — yes, DEFAULTS.configPath line 20. ✓\n2. \"AC-046 requires select 路由的输出与 CLI 一致\" — yes from prompt. ✓\n3. \"interfaces §5 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 只出现在 draft 视图里\" — yes, line 15 of interfaces.md: \"兼容的选模拒选原因 E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION 只出现在 draft 视图里\". ✓\n4. \"interfaces §2 rejected.reason enum\" — line 8: \"rejected.reason 枚举：excluded, level_mismatch, ... reserve_protected\" — no E_FORECAST_EXHAUSTION. ✓\n5. \"§7 sort by 剩余量 / 距重置小时数\" — design §7 rule 2. ✓\n6. \"AC-007 按剩余任务数排序生效\" — yes. ✓\n7. \"§6 没有样本时用配置估计值\" — yes. ✓\n8. \"§9 缺样本一律显示 unknown\" — yes. ✓\n9. \"AC-008 缺容量或缺样本时 risk 保持 unknown\" — yes. ✓\n10. \"forbidden-word list contains cli\" — §3: \"确认不出现 cli、provider、vendor、模型 id、价格、额度、forecast 或直接调用命令\". ✓ And wrapped call is `node <pkg>/bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease <id> --config <cfg>`. Contains \"cliworker\" and \"conf