ll` currently, to be flipped). The test-strategy flagged this as important (\"否则 A 系列修复没有回归网\"). Since the reviewer should review the design+task graph+matrix (and the test architecture), I can note that the task graph doesn't include characterization/golden tests for A-series bugs, which the test architect recommends. That's a legitimate finding. Let me fold it into F-09 or F-02. I'll add it to F-09 (errata/goldens) or make a separate minor. Let me fold into F-09: \"AC-044/045 是全新功能而非回归，需另立金标；且 T-001~005 未包含对 A 系列缺陷的 characterization/golden 测试（test-strategy §2），重构后无回归锚点\".\n\nActually, let me keep F-09 focused and add characterization as part of F-02 (contract freeze / milestone rework). Hmm. I'll add a short clause to F-09.\n\nLet me also double-check: does the design/graph mention `scripts/run-tests.mjs` enumerating `**/*.test.mjs` and excluding fixtures/helpers? T-001 outputs `scripts/run-tests.mjs（枚举文件后调用 node --test）` and `scripts/check-test-discovery.mjs`. test-strategy §3 says must explicitly exclude `test/fixtures/` and `test/helpers/`. The task graph T-011/T-012/T-013 add `test/fixtures/**` and `test/helpers/**` with `.mjs` files (fakecli.mjs, make-shims.mjs, fs-probe.mjs) — these are NOT `.test.mjs` so a `**/*.test.mjs` glob wouldn't pick them up anyway. But `test/fixtures/adapters/**` goldens are `.json`, fine. However there's `test/unit/discovery/**` and `test/integration/...` — all `.test.mjs`. So the exclusion is defensive. test-strategy §3 also wants \"集合相等断言\" (set equality) rather than count equality — AC-001 says \"执行数与文件数一致（check-test-discovery 校验）\" — count equality, not set equality. TB-4/test-strategy §3 explicitly recommends set equality. AC-001's wording \"执行数与文件数一致\" is weaker. That's a real minor gap: count equality can pass while a file is silently skipped and another double-run. Let me include that in F-13 or a separate finding. Let me add to F-13 (tooling) — actually it's more of an AC quality issue. Let me put it in F-04 (wall-clock/CI