{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5cb-d873-7683-bff1-59cc5c723990","session_id":"01a1b5ca-cb08-780f-9329-83341daeb0e2","message":{"id":"01a1b5cbd8737683bff159ca4d4738de","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The config.mjs:19 confirmed:\n- `if (!raw || raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA) throw new Error(\\`unsupported CLIWorker config schema: ${raw.schema}\\`)` — when raw is null, `!raw` short-circuits to true, so the AND part isn't evaluated, but the template literal `${raw.schema}` IS evaluated in the throw message → TypeError. Confirmed. And no `error.code = 'E_CONFIG'` on lines 19-21. Confirmed. So the designer's 勘误 #1 is accurate.\n\n- `.gitignore`: has 3 lines actually (config/cliworker.local.json, usage.jsonl, node_modules/). The designer said \"现在只有字面的 config/cliworker.local.json 和 usage.jsonl 两行，没有通配\" — actually there's node_modules/ as a third line. Minor discrepancy. But effectively no wildcards. AC-013 expects git check-ignore to hit config/a.local.json, state/x, a.jsonl — currently none would match. Confirmed the design's intent.\n\n- `.collab/` files EXIST on disk (Glob found them). But are they tracked? Glob shows files on disk, not tracking. TB-6 claims `.collab/` is untracked (from logs). I can't run git ls-files. Let me check if there's a way... I can't use Bash. Maybe I can look at .git/index? That's binary. Hmm.\n\nActually, TB-6 says \".collab/ 在上一轮日志中记为未跟踪\" (recorded as untracked in last round's logs). Let me check the logs to see. Let me read the designer.log, test_architect.log, reviewer.log, state.json, and interfaces.md (at least headers), review-v1.verdict.json.\n\nLet me read these to verify the claims and understand the authoritative spec situation.\n\nAlso let me read lib/select.mjs (forecast call points), lib/forecast.mjs, lib/cli.mjs, package.json, dsh.plugin.json, config/cliworker.example.json.\n\nLet me batch reads.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message