{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b61c-9ebf-7bf5-b477-033bab47f656","session_id":"01a1b616-1026-7677-9977-23fa65c09949","message":{"id":"01a1b61c9ebf7bf5b47703396e797b44","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very helpful. interfaces.md section 【1】 says:\n\n\"draft 视图：不带 schema 或带 compat:'draft' 时得到 draft 视图并带 W_DRAFT_DEPRECATED，0.3.0 移除；CLI 允许 draft，HTTP 上 draft 与 view:'full' 都需要有效会话，否则返回 403 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN；CLI 的 models select 带 view:'full' 返回 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN，完整视图只在 admin select。\"\n\nSo: on HTTP, draft (no schema or compat:draft) AND view:full both need a valid session, else 403 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN. So §7's \"HTTP 上没有 schema 也视为 draft，所以同样需要会话\" matches interfaces.md. And the route table \"POST /cliworker/select 不需要会话；请求带 view:'full' 或 compat:'draft'，而没有有效会话时返回 403 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN\" — this mentions only view:full/compat:draft, omitting \"no schema → draft\". But interfaces.md says \"不带 schema 或带 compat:'draft' 时得到 draft 视图\" and \"HTTP 上 draft 与 view:'full' 都需要有效会话\".\n\nSo there IS a real inconsistency: the HTTP route table (§7) and AC-059 say \"POST /cliworker/select 无 view 返回 200 AgentLine 视图\" — but a plain AgentLine request with no `schema` field is \"不带 schema\" = draft, which per interfaces.md and §7 CLI section requires a session on HTTP → E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN. \n\nNow, is \"无 view\" the same as \"不带 schema\"? AC-059: \"POST /cliworker/select 无 view 返回 200 AgentLine 视图且 scan 0 命中\". A request could have no view but have schema:'cliworker.request/v1' → normal request → 200. A request with no view AND no schema → draft → 403 per interfaces/§7. So AC-059's \"无 view 返回 200\" implicitly assumes schema present. But the design's §7 CLI line says \"HTTP 上没有 schema 也视为 draft，所以同样需要会话\" — meaning ANY no-schema request needs a session. \n\nHmm, but wait: does the AgentLine POST /cliworker/select carry `schema`? Per 【1】, the ModelRequest v1 includes `{schema:'cliworker.request/v1', ...}`. So a proper AgentLine request HAS a schema. So the \"no schema → draft\" rule applies only to requests that omit the schema field, which are legacy/draft requests. So there's no contradiction for proper v1 requests: they have schema, no view → 200 AgentLine. OK! So actually the design is consistent: \n- schema present, no view → 200 AgentLine (AC-059 row 1) ✓\n- no schema (draft) or compat:draft or view:full, no session → 403 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN ✓\n- CLI: no schema/compat:draft → allowed with W_DRAFT_DEPRECATED; view:full → E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN ✓\n\nSo my potential \"contradiction\" is resolved by the fact that v1 requests carry `schema`. But — is this clearly stated in §7? §7 says \"HTTP 上没有 schema 也视为 draft，所以同样需要会话\" — yes, it is stated. And AC-059's \"无 view 返回 200\" is about v1 requests. OK. So no contradiction. Good, I won't raise it. Actually, hmm, but there's still ambiguity: AC-059's row 1 says \"无 view 返回 200\" without saying \"with schema\". A test could send a no-schema, no-view request and expect 200 per AC-059 but 403 per §7. That's a latent ambiguity but minor, and arguably a test-design detail. I'll not raise it — the 6 TBs are stronger. Actually, hmm, but F-08 was specifically about \"每个触发条件只对应一个错误码\" and unique trigger conditions. This draft/session overlap (view:full, compat:draft, no-schema all → E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN) is three triggers for one code — but that's fine (one code, multiple trigger conditions, each trigger has one code). Actually AC-009 says \"每个码带唯一的 trigger_id\" — E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN with 3 trigger conditions might need 3 trigger_ids or one combined. Hmm, minor. Not worth a finding.\n\nLet me now also double-check TB-1's claim about AC-061 more carefully. AC-061 text: \"doctor 与 /cliworker/health 都报告：配置有效性、state_dir 是否可写、锁状态、密钥后端、清单年龄、过期探测数量、注册状态、test_clock。注入任一故障（含设置 CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE）时，doctor 以 E_HEALTH_DEGRADED 退出（退出码 9），health 返回 status degraded 并列出故障项。\"\n\nSo \"test_clock\" is a reported item, and setting the clock file is an injected fault → degraded. §0.1: \"只要设置了该变量，CLI 每次输出都带 W_TEST_CLOCK，health 也会报告