clock\" but changes status to degraded. Meanwhile §0.1 doesn't say status degraded. So the design leaves health's status ambiguous when the var is set. That's the gap: \"钉死该变量对 health/doctor 的语义\" is a valid ask. OK, I'll confirm TB-1 but perhaps soften the \"opposite conclusions\" language in my finding text to be precise: the variable is used both as a normal cross-process fixture (AC-064/072, W_TEST_CLOCK as expected warning) and as an injected degradation fault (AC-061, E_HEALTH_DEGRADED), without pinning whether health/doctor should treat it as normal/test-mode or degraded, and AC-064/072 don't assert health status. Plus the mode-mixing and env-isolation gaps. I'll write my own precise text.\n\nNow let me also double check TB-2's claim: \"没有任何对 contracts/golden/** 与 contracts/spec/** 的哈希清单或 check-golden-frozen 进入 check-fast\". Let me check AC-073 and §4 again. AC-073: \"权威规格自包含：contracts/registry.snapshot.json、contracts/spec/*.json、contracts/golden/** 都已被 git 跟踪（git ls-files 列出），并通过各自的 schema 校验；check-no-collab...；gen-contract-doc 重新生成的 docs/contract.md 与已提交版本逐字节一致；registry.snapshot.json 含 interfaces 第 5 节的全部码...\" — no hash freeze. §4: \"金标由 T-004 一次写定，后续任务的 write_scope 不包含 contracts/golden。要改金标只能走蓝图变更，并递增 snapshot_version。\" — this is a RULE but no automated enforcement. AC-010's compareRegistry + snapshot_version only covers registry.snapshot.json. So yes, TB-2 is valid: nothing enforces golden immutability. Confirmed. \n\nIs there any check that enforces write_scope? Let me search the task graph for \"check-write-scope\" or similar. Looking at scripts in T-001's outputs: check-test-discovery, check-fast, check-traceability, check-ci, milestone-gate, check-defects, gen-ci. T-004: snapshot-update, gen-contract-doc, check-contract-doc, check-no-collab. No check-write-scope. AC-004's check-traceability validates shards, not write_scope. So no enforcement. TB-2 confirmed.\n\nTB-3: Let me verify \"AC-001/AC-002 把 skips.jsonl 单独上传，却未定义 files-executed.json 是否包含全跳过文