s M1 too, and by the time M1 gate runs, both tasks are done. Unless T-007's part is omitted. The concern is legitimate but somewhat mitigated. Still, the multi-owner + single [fixed] design is a real ambiguity: who owns the file, and does \"具备 [fixed]\" mean one section or per-owner sections? I'd confirm but maybe rate \"major\". \n\nActually, wait — there's a more serious angle: two tasks (T-006 and T-007) BOTH have \"test/characterization/defects/a1-quota.test.mjs\" in their write_scope. That's a WRITE CONFLICT — two tasks writing the same file. In a task-graph-driven implementation (likely parallel agents), two agents editing the same file is a real coordination problem. §5 says \"[fixed] 部分针对 live lib，由归属任务补写\" — but a1-quota has TWO owner tasks. So the design is internally inconsistent: defects.json has one owner_task but a1-quota is listed with two. TB-4 captures this. Confirmed.\n\nTB-5: Let me verify \"check-frozen-files 只覆盖 v0.1/ 与 stable.test.mjs\". AC-005: \"frozen-files.json 只登记副本文件与 stable.test.mjs 的 sha256；check-frozen-files 在哈希变化时失败，在清单出现任何其他路径（包括 lib 下的路径）时也失败\" — yes. \"[repro] 永远运行、永远应当通过\" ✓ §5. No mutation canary ✓ (no mention anywhere). \"T-002 写 [repro]、后续属主任务在同一文件追加 [fixed]\" ✓ (§5: \"每个缺陷文件的 [repro] 部分...；[fixed] 部分...由归属任务补写\" — same file). So the [repro] section can be weakened by any task that writes [fixed] to the same file, with no integrity check. Valid. Confirmed. Severity: this undermines the whole characterization regression value. Major or blocking. I'd say major.\n\nTB-6: verified above. Confirmed.\n\nSo all 6 TBs are valid (with TB-1's \"opposite conclusions\" being a mild overstatement but the underlying gaps real). I'll confirm all 6 as \"open\". \n\nNow, do I have any additional findings of my own? Let me think about a couple more consistency checks:\n\n(a) **§0.2 vs §4 vs T-004 write_scope** — TB-6 covers.\n\n(b) **AC-073 requires \"contracts/spec/*.json ... 通过各自的 schema 校验\"** — but `contracts/spec/ac-index.json` is written by T-001, and T-004's `test/contract/spec-tracked.test.mjs` checks it. Do the schemas exist for ac-index.json? T-004 outputs \"contracts/schemas/**\" — presumably including ac-index schema. Not specified, minor. Not worth a finding.\n\n(c) **AC-004: \"baseline 与层级相容（unit、contract、integration、e2e 只能取 linux、win32、darwin；smoke 只能取 linux 或 real-smoke）\"** — but §6 says \"smoke 只能取 linux（dry-run）或 real-smoke\" and AC-069 is smoke with linux baseline (dry-run). OK. But what about AC-038 (smoke, real-smoke)? Compatible. What about the CI matrix: \"CI 基线：对应 OS 的 runner 上，任一 Node 版本至少有一次 pass\" — for real-smoke AC, CI baseline isn't used; only real smoke report. OK.\n\nHmm, one thing: AC-070 says \"某条 AC 在 ac-index 声明的 baseline 上只有 skip 时阻断\". For win32-baseline AC-027, on ubuntu runner it's skipped — but that's fine because its baseline is win32, so the ubuntu run's skip doesn't matter; only the windows runner's pass counts. OK.\n\n(d) **AC-072: \"真实 createContext 在设置 CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE 时 now() 返回文件中的值\"** — but §3 says the real clock's now() reads the file, AND \"定时器仍用真实时间\". AC-028 uses `advance(timeout_ms)` — which requires the fake clock. So AC-028 must use injected fake clock (ctx overrides), not the real createContext with env var. The design's AC table (§3) maps AC-028 → advance, AC-029 → advance, AC-064 → file clock. So no test mixes. But AC-072 sets the env var IN-PROCESS to test createContext, then checks \"未设置时不出现该警告\". If AC-072's test sets the env var and doesn't restore, and the full test suite runs in one process... Actually `run-tests` probably spawns `node --test` per file or one process. If one process, leakage. TB-1 covers this.\n\n(e) **W_TEST_CLOCK in \"每个输出\"** — §0: \"CLI 每次输出都带 W_TEST_CLOCK\". But AC-023 requires \"除 run 外，每个 CLI 命令的完整 stdout 都能被 JSON.parse 解析为单个值\" — an extra warning field is still valid JSON, so OK. But AC-015/016/017/051 deep-equal goldens — those are pure function outputs, not CLI outputs. OK. But AC-024: \"README 中所有请求示例交给解析器后 warnings 都为空\" — parser, not CLI output. OK. Hmm, what about AC-056 \"models select 带 view:full 返回 E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN（退出码 2）\" — error output with W_TEST_CLOCK? Only if env set. OK.\n\nActually — here's a thought: W_TEST_CLOCK appended to \"每个输出\" could break AC-059's HTTP response deep-equality checks? AC-059 checks status and code, not exact body. OK. And leak-scan? No.\n\n(f) **check-seams ban on `node:timers` outside lib/context.mjs** — but `test/helpers/clock.mjs` implements the fake clock. Does the fake clock need `setTimeout`? It's a virtual clock, so no. But the REAL clock in lib/context.mjs uses global timers. OK. However — §0.1 says \"ctx.clock 提供 now()、setTimeout、clearTimeout、sleep\" — but the fake clock also has advance/setNow/pending. The real clock's setTimeout maps to global setTimeout. Fine. But here's a subtle issue: `check-seams` bans \"全局 setTimeout、setInterval、setImmediate 和 node:timers\" outside lib/context.mjs. But `lib/exec.mjs` (T-010) implements timeouts \"经 ctx.clock\" ✓. `lib/lock.mjs` uses ctx.clock.sleep ✓. OK.\n\n(g) **AC-028: \"advance(timeout_ms)\" but §3 says file-clock mode uses real timers** — AC-028 uses the fake clock. OK.\n\n(h) **The `main()` \"在每个输出里追加 W_TEST_CLOCK\"** — but AC-006 says \"在子进程中 import lib/cli.mjs 与 lib/index.js：stdout 和 stderr 都是 0 字节\" — import doesn't call main. OK.\n\n(i) **F-03 residual: AC-038 assigned to T-029 with levels=[smoke], baseline real-smoke. But AC-038's text says \"smoke-real 的 wsl-discover 步骤（ac:['AC-038']）...步骤状态为 pass\" and \"dry-run 中同名步骤使用夹具，其 pass 不计入 real-smoke 基线\". AC-069 (dry-run smoke) includes \"wsl-discover（夹具）\" step with ac field. But which AC does the dry-run wsl-discover step declare? If it declares AC-038, then the dry-run report would show a pass step for AC-038 — but AC-070 says \"dry-run 报告永远不能满足 real-smoke\". And AC-038 says \"dry-run 中同名步骤使用夹具，其 pass 不计入 real-smoke 基线\" — consistent with AC-070. But does AC-069 require wsl-discover step to have an `ac` field? AC-069: \"每个步骤声明 ac 字段\". If wsl-discover dry-run step declares ac:['AC-038'], then the release-gate must ignore dry-run reports for real-smoke — it does (\"dry-run 报告不能满足\"). OK. But hmm — if the dry-run wsl-discover step declares ac:['AC-038'] and dry-run reports are mode:'dry-run', AC-070 says real-smoke baseline only accepts mode:'real'. So ignored. OK.\n\nBut wait, what about AC-069's own baseline? If AC-069 is smoke with baseline linux (dry-run), then the dry-run report's steps with ac:['AC-069']? AC-069 says \"每个步骤声明 ac 字段，全部 pass，生成通过 cliworker.smoke/v1 校验的报告（mode dry-run）\". Hmm — which AC do the steps declare? If all 7 steps declare ac:['AC-069'], then AC-069's pass source is the dry-run report. But AC-070 says \"dry-run 报告永远不能满足 real-smoke\" — that's fine for AC-069 (baseline linux). But does release-gate accept dry-run reports for linux-baseline smoke AC? AC-070: \"CI 基线：对应 OS 的 runner 上，任一 Node 版本至少有一次 pass\" and \"real-smoke 基线：只认 mode real...\". Hmm — for a linux-baseline smoke AC (AC-069), is the pass source the CI runner (files-executed + reporter) or the dry-run smoke report? The design says \"smoke 只能取 linux（dry-run）或 real-smoke\". So linux baseline is for dry-run. But release-gate's \"CI 基线\" requires \"对应 OS 的 runner 上，任一 Node 版本至少有一次 pass\" — from files-executed.json/reporter results. And the dry-run smoke report? AC-070 doesn't explicitly say how linux-baseline smoke ACs get their pass. Hmm! AC-069 is a smoke-level AC whose test is `test/smoke/smoke-dry-run.test.mjs` which runs in CI on all OSes. So AC-069 gets a pass from the CI reporter (like any other test). OK, so no issue. The dry-run smoke report is for real-smoke mapping, not for AC-069. Fine.\n\nOK, I'm fairly confident the 6 TBs are the main findings. Let me also consider whether I should raise a finding about **§0.2 \"这些文件都由 T-004...实现任务只读不写\" conflicting with T-001 being an implementation task that writes ac-index.json** — that's TB-6, covered.\n\nOne more: **AC-073 says \"contracts/spec/*.