al-smoke, requiring a real WSL machine. AC-038 is in T-029's acceptance. But T-029's acceptance_direction says \"CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1 node scripts/smoke-real.mjs --out <报告文件>（维护者在装有 WSL 的 Windows 真机上运行）\". And milestone-gate --milestone M5 requires \"属主任务在 Mx 及以前的 AC 全部 covered，并且在完整运行中通过\". AC-038 is in M5 (T-029) with baseline real-smoke — can M5 gate require it to pass \"在完整运行中通过\"? AC-038's pass source is a real smoke report on a maintainer's machine, not the CI full run. §6 milestone-gate: \"属主任务在 Mx 及以前的 AC 全部 covered，并且在完整运行中通过\". Hmm — for AC-038 (real-smoke), \"在完整运行中通过\" would be impossible in CI. But §6 also says \"不校验更晚里程碑的 AC\". AC-038 is M5, so M5 gate WOULD check it. Hmm. Is there a contradiction? AC-074 says \"milestone-gate --milestone Mx 只要求属主里程碑 <= Mx 的 AC 为 covered 并在完整运行中通过\". So M5 gate requires AC-038 covered AND passed in full run. But AC-038's baseline is real-smoke, whose pass source is a real smoke report (or waiver). Can milestone-gate accept a waiver? §6: \"豁免...只适用于 baseline 为 real-smoke 的 AC...在报告中单独列为 waived\" — that's release-gate, not milestone-gate. So milestone-gate --milestone M5 might block AC-038 permanently without a real WSL machine. Hmm! \n\nActually, §0.3 says \"豁免只认仓库内 release/waivers.json 的显式条目，只适用于 baseline 为 real-smoke 的 AC，单列报告，不算通过\". And §6 release-gate handles waivers. But milestone-gate (§6) doesn't mention waivers or real-smoke special handling. AC-074 and AC-070 (release-gate) are separate. So there's a potential gap: milestone-gate M5 requires ALL ACs (including AC-038 real-smoke) \"covered 并在完整运行中通过\" — but AC-038 can never \"在完整运行中通过\" (it needs a real WSL machine). Unless the dry-run smoke test `test/smoke/wsl-discover.test.mjs` (report entry validation) counts as \"在完整运行中通过\" for AC-038's test file. Hmm — T-029 outputs \"test/smoke/wsl-discover.test.mjs（报告条目校验）\" which IS a unit-ish test that runs in CI. So AC-038's TEST FILE can pass in the full run (it validates report entries using fixtures), while the real-smoke baseline pass comes from the real report. So \"在完整运行中通过\" might refer to the test file passing, not the baseline. Ambiguous but probably OK. Not a clean finding. I'll skip.\n\nHmm, but actually this connects to TB-3 (all-skipped files) — on non-Windows CI, would wsl-discover.test.mjs be all-skipped? It's \"报告条目校验\" (report entry validation) which should run with fixtures on any OS. So not skipped. OK.\n\nAlright, I'll also consider: is there a finding about **§6 \"CI 基线：对应 OS 的 runner 上，任一 Node 版本至少有一次 pass\"** combined with real-smoke AC-038 having no CI pass? AC-070's release-gate handles baseline-specific logic. For real-smoke baseline, the pass source is the real report — not CI. But §6 says \"每条 AC 的 baseline 都来自 ac-index\" and \"CI 基线：对应 OS 的 runner 上，任一 Node 版本至少有一次 pass\" — this is stated generally. For real-smoke ACs, the CI baseline rule would require a pass on the OS runner, which is impossible. But the next bullet defines \"real-smoke 基线\" separately. So presumably baseline-specific rules apply. AC-070 tests \"某条 AC 在 ac-index 声明的 baseline 上只有 skip 时阻断\" and \"real-smoke 基线只认 mode real...\". So release-gate has baseline-specific handling. OK, not a clean finding.\n\nI'll go with 8 findings total: 6 confirmed TBs (F-01..F-06), 1 new dependency finding (F-07), 1 resolved catch-all (F-08).\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider whether adding my own new finding is wise. The user asked me to be the reviewer and produce a verdict. Adding a well-founded independent finding strengthens the review. The dependency gap is concrete and verifiable. I'll include it. But I should make sure I'm right about T-002's depends_on. Let me re-read from the inline task graph:\n\n\"T-002\": \"depends_on\": [\"T-001\"], \"inputs\": [\"git show f75bb76 下的 lib 与 config/cliworker.example.json\", \"contracts/spec/surfaces.json 的保留面清单（与 T-004 共同约定，由 T-004 写入）\", \"第 2 节勘误\"].\n\nYes. And T-004 \"depends_on\": [\"T-001\"]. So no path from T-002 to T-004. Confirmed.\n\nAlso note: T-002's acceptance is AC-005, which requires surfaces.json. And T-004's acceptance includes AC-073 (spec tracked). Both M1. If executed in ID order (common in task graphs), T-002 runs before T-004 → AC-005 cannot pass. Solid.\n\nSeverity: major. Status: open.\n\nHmm, but actually — is there a chance the designer intends surfaces.json to exist before M1 tasks start (e.g., \"与 T-004 共同约定\" meaning agreed in the blueprint phase, and the file is committed as part of the blueprint)? §0.2 says \"这些文件都由 T-004 在 M1 写入并提交\" — explicitly written by T-004 during M1. So no. Confirmed.\n\nOK. Now let me also reconsider the resolved catch-all: with 7 open findings (6 TB + 1 new), is \"resolved\" finding appropriate? Yes, it's a catch-all acknowledging what was verified, like v2's F-09. I'll keep it but make it concise and explicitly scoped.\n\nActually, hmm — let me reconsider. If I include a \"resolved\" finding that says \"F-01..F-08 核心处理成立\" but 6 of my open findings are residual gaps IN those fixes, a strict reader might see tension. But I'll phrase it as \"核心机制已落地，但以下 7 项为新引入机制的残留/遗漏缺口\" — that's coherent. Good.\n\nLet me now reconsider severities one final time:\n- F-01 (TB-1 clock): major\n- F-02 (TB-2 golden freeze): blocking\n- F-03 (TB-3 set equality): major\n- F-04 (TB-4 a1-quota): major\n- F-05 (TB-5 repro canary): blocking\n- F-06 (TB-6 ac-index owner): major\n- F-07 (T-002 dep): major\n- F-08 (resolved catch-all): minor, resolved\n\nHmm, 2 blocking, 5 major, 1 minor. That's a lot of majors. Fine. Actually, let me reconsider F-01 → maybe blocking given F-01 original was blocking and clock underlies ≥8 ACs. But the residual is about the additive file-clock mechanism. I'll keep major. Actually, let me bump TB-3 to blocking? \"在 3 OS 矩阵上不可实现\" — hmm. I'll keep major; it's a definitional fix. \n\nHmm, one concern: should I mark any finding as \"disputed\"? The format offers it. I don't dispute any TB. I'll leave all open. That's fine.\n\nLet me now finalize the JSON. I must output ONLY the JSON object, no code fences, no prose. Let me make sure the text strings are properly escaped (no unescaped quotes/newlines). I'll use Chinese punctuation and avoid double quotes inside text. I'll use 「」 or '' for quoting. Let me use single quotes or 「」 to be safe. Actually JSON strings can contain single quotes fine; double quotes must be escaped. I'll use 「」 and '' and avoid \" entirely. Also avoid backslashes.\n\nLet me write it carefully.\n\nOne more check: the example shows `\"id\":\"F-01\"` etc. I'll use F-01..F-08.\n\nLet me draft the final JSON:\n\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"F-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"status\":\"open\",\"text\":\"...\"},\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n\nLet me write each text carefully, concise but with concrete references.\n\nF-01: \"确认 TB-1（时钟夹具与降级故障未钉死）：§0.1/§3 规定设置 CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE 时 main() 每个输出追加 W_TEST_CLOCK、health 报告 test_clock，且 now() 读文件而定时器仍走真实时间；但 AC-061 把「设置该变量」列为注入故障，要求 doctor 退出 E_HEALTH_DEGRADED(9)、health 返回 degraded，AC-072 又在进程内设置/撤销它验证重读与警告，AC-064 只在子进程 env 设置。同一变量既是正常跨进程夹具又是降级故障，health/doctor 是否应判 degraded 未澄清；§3 未声明它与伪时钟模式互斥、未禁止混用，也未写明文件模式只提供虚拟 now()+真实定时器、不支持 advance/sleep 的虚拟推进（AC-028/029 依赖 advance）。另外 W_TEST_CLOCK 进入「每个输出」叠加进程级 env 泄漏：AC-072 若不在 finally 恢复，check-fast 末尾那次完整 npm test 的深相等断言会被污染，设计无泄漏 canary。须钉死该变量对 health/doctor 的语义、只在子进程 env 注入并 finally 恢复、补无泄漏 canary、写明两种时钟模式互斥。\"\n\nF-02: \"确认 TB-2（金标 oracle 可静默漂移）：§4 称金标由 T-004 一次写定、后续 write_scope 不含 contracts/golden、改动须走蓝图变更并递增 snapshot_version，但 AC-073 只校验 git 跟踪 + 各自 schema + check-no-collab + docs/contract.md 逐字节一致，AC-010 的 compareRegistry 与 snapshot_version 递增只覆盖 registry.snapshot.json；既无 contracts/golden/** 与 contracts/spec/** 的逐文件 sha256 冻结清单，也无 check-golden-frozen 纳入 check-fast，更无检查器强制 write_scope。后续任务可直接改金标 input/expected 让 AC-015/016/017/050/051 的深相等断言「通过」而无人察觉，正好架空 F-02 的权威规格入库。须补随仓库提交的逐文件哈希清单、纳入 check-fast 的校验器，明确 snapshot_version 对全部规格文件递增，并钉死由哪个 check 强制 write_scope。\"\n\nF-03: \"确认 TB-3（完整运行集合相等在三 OS 矩阵上未定义全跳过文件）：AC-001 要求完整运行写 files-executed.json(mode:full) 并当场断言「枚举集合 == reporter 实际执行集合」，AC-002 把 skips.jsonl 单独上传却未定义二者关系；AC-027 非 win32 写跳过记录、AC-033 原生后端按平台门控、AC-038 dry-run 等会产生「文件已枚举但用例全 skip」。若 reporter 的「实际执行集合」不含全跳过文件，ubuntu/macos 的完整运行必然因集合不等失败，而 check-test-discovery 的夹具只覆盖不一致检出、filtered 不能顶替、fixtures 下 x.test.mjs 不执行，无全跳过 canary。须明确 files-executed.json 记录的是「已加载的测试文件」、skip 只进 skips.jsonl，并补全跳过文件 canary，否则 F-06 的集合相等不可实现。\"\n\nF-04: \"确认 TB-4（a1-quota 双属主令里程碑翻转误判）：§5 把 a1-quota 记为 T-006/T-007 两个属主，T-006 写「预测部分 [fixed]」、T-007 写「draft 部分 [fixed]」，两者 write_scope 都含 test/characterization/defects/a1-quota.test.mjs（写冲突），AC-021 也要求该文件 [fixed] 通过；但 defects.json 每条只有一个 owner_task，§5 的缺陷文件只有单一 [repro]/[fixed] 两段，check-defects 与 AC-074/milestone-gate 只检查「具备 [fixed] 部分」是否存在。任一任务先补分段，即便另一半（预测公式或 Heavy 拒选）无断言，M1 门也会判已翻转。须把 a1-quota 拆成两条缺陷，或把 [fixed] 按 owner_task 分子段并让 check-defects/milestone-gate 校验每个属主分段都存在且含对应 [AC-xxx] 标题，同时消除两任务写同一文件的冲突。\"\n\nF-05: \"确认 TB-5（缺陷档案可静默架空）：AC-005/§5 要求 [repro]「永远运行、永远应当通过」，但没有变异 canary（用已修复的 v0.1 副本变体跑每条 repro 必须失败）证明它真能检出缺陷——恒真、删空或改成无关断言都不会被发现；且 T-002 写 [repro]、后续属主任务在同一文件追加 [fixed]，而 frozen-files.json/check-frozen-files 只登记 v0.1/ 与 stable.test.mjs 的 sha256，[repro] 段不受任何哈希校验，可被顺手改写。于是 M5「11 条全部具备 [fixed]」也可能以空断言达成，F-04 的保留面锁定与 F-05 的翻转门禁同时失去回归价值。须为每类缺陷补变异 canary，并把 repro 与 fixed 拆成两个文件（或给 [repro] 段登记哈希由 check-defects 校验）。\"\n\nF-06: \"确认 TB-6（ac-index.json 属主三处矛盾）：§0 第 2 条写「contracts/spec/ 放 AC 索引、保留面…这些文件都由 T-004 在 M1 写入并提交，实现任务只读不写」，把 ac-index.json 也归 T-004；但 §4 表格与任务图/验收矩阵把 contracts/spec/ac-index.json 钉给 T-001（T-001 write_scope 含它，T-004 只有 surfaces.json、migration-map.json 与 golden/**），AC-001/004/070/074 与 F-06 的「单一 AC 索引、baseline 唯一声明」全依赖唯一写入者。照 §0 理解由 T-004 再写一份，或实现任务按「只读不写」反向去写，都会破坏单一事实来源。须把属主钉死为 T-001，统一 §0/§4/任务图三处表述并显式声明 T-004 不写该文件。\"\n\nF-07: \"新增（T-002 缺 T-004 依赖，与 F-06 同类的依赖闭合遗漏）：T-002 的 inputs 明列「contracts/spec/surfaces.json 的保留面清单（由 T-004 写入）」，AC-005 也要求 stable.test.mjs 锁定 surfaces.json 列出的保留面，§0 第 4 条同样把该文件归 T-004 写入；但 T-002 depends_on 只有 T-001，T-004 也只依赖 T-001，二者同属 M1 且无传递路径，按 ID 序或并行执行时 T-002 会早于 surfaces.json 存在就跑 AC-005。T-030 的依赖已按 F-06 补齐，T-002 这一处仍漏。须给 T-002 增加 depends_on T-004，并复核其余消费 contracts/spec 与 contracts/golden 的任务是否都有到 T-004 的依赖路径。\"\n\nF-08: \"已核验、核心处理成立：上一轮 8 条意见的核心机制均已在第三轮稿、任务图与验收矩阵实质落地——可推进时钟与 check-seams（AC-072、手段表）、自包含 registry.snapshot.json 与 contracts/spec+golden 入库（AC-073、AC-015/016/017/051 读金标、check-no-collab）、real-smoke 基线与 wsl-discover 步骤 ac 映射/豁免（AC-038/069/070）、只冻结 0.1 副本（AC-005）、M1 改名与 milestone-gate（AC-074）、单一 ac-index 与仅完整运行做集合比较（AC-001/004）、session/ui 例外与 csrf 随会话签发（AC-059/060）、trigger_id 唯一与 E_LOOPBACK_ONLY 及单码路由表（AC-009）。本轮 revise 仅针对上述 F-01..F-07 的新增残留/遗漏缺口，不是对整体修订的否定。\"\n\nGood. Let me double-check JSON escaping: I used 「」 and 『』 — those are fine in JSON. I used '': no double quotes. I used parentheses (9) — fine. I used \"/\" and \".\" — fine. I used \"==\" — fine. No backslashes except in file paths like \"contracts/golden/**\" — forward slashes, fine. \"test/characterization/defects/a1-quota.test.mjs\" — fine. No double quotes inside strings. Good.\n\nWait, in F-07 I wrote \"按 ID 序或并行执行时 T-002 会早于 surfaces.json 存在就跑 AC-005\" — slightly awkward but understandable. Let me refine: \"按 ID 序或并行执行时 surfaces.json 尚未生成 T-002 就要跑 AC-005\". Better.\n\nAlso F-08: I reference \"上述 F-01..F-07\" — meaning MY findings F-01..F-07. But it says \"上一轮 8 条意见\" separately. Slight ambiguity but OK. Let me phrase \"本轮 revise 仅针对 F-01..F-07 列举的新增残留/遗漏缺口\". Good.\n\nHmm, one thing: F-08's severity \"minor\" with status \"resolved\" — consistent with v2's F-09 (minor, resolved). Good.\n\nNow, should the final answer include ONLY this JSON? Yes. No code fences, no prose. Let me also make sure I don't add a trailing summary.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the plan-mode constraint one last time. The system reminder says my turn should end with asking a question or calling ExitPlanMode, and that I should write a plan file. But the user explicitly said \"不要修改、创建或删除任何文件\" (don't modify/create/delete any files) and \"请只输出一个 JSON 对象\". Creating a plan file would violate the user's explicit instruction. And ExitPlanMode is for implementation tasks, not review/research tasks (\"For research tasks... do NOT use this tool\"). This is a read-only review whose deliverable is a JSON verdict in the response text. So I will NOT create a plan file and will NOT call ExitPlanMode. I'll just output the JSON. \n\nThis is the right call: user's explicit current instruction (only output a JSON, no file changes) overrides the generic plan-mode workflow, and the plan-mode instructions themselves say ExitPlanMode is only for implementation tasks requiring writing code. Also, \"you MUST NOT make any edits (with the exception of the plan file)\" — I made no edits at all, which is fully compliant.\n\nLet me finalize. Actually, let me reconsider finding IDs once more — I want to reduce risk. Given the example `{\"id\":\"F-01\",...}` and review-v2's fresh numbering pattern, F-01..F-08 fresh is right. Good.\n\nLet me produce the final JSON, carefully formatted (single object, valid JSON). I'll keep it compact but readable.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b61613ff7aa18485436ab5d61d70","_messageId":"01a1b61c9ebf7bf5b47703396e797b44","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b61613ff7aa18485436ab5d61d70","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b61c9ebf7bf5b47703396e797b44","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b61c9ebf7bf5b47703396e797b44","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b61c-9ebf-7bf5-b477-033bab47f656","traceparent":"00-0659ed5c3929267d759b8c952231eadd-a9a9a88101c02c28-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b616-1026-7677-9977-23fa65c09949,codebuddy.conversation_re